msgid ""
"Here is another example that asks the user for the `Notification permission "
"<https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Notifications_API>`__ and "
"waits asynchronously to deliver a notification if the permission is granted:"
msgstr ""
"Aquí hi ha un altre exemple que demana a l'usuari el `Permís de notificació "
"<https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Notifications_API>`__ i "
"espera de manera asíncrona per lliurar una notificació si es concedeix el "
"permís:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:137
msgid "Can I use my favorite library?"
msgstr "Puc utilitzar la meva biblioteca preferida?"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:139
msgid ""
"You most likely can. First, you have to include your library in the page. "
"You can customize the :ref:`Head Include <doc_javascript_export_options>` "
"during export (see below), or even :ref:`write your own template "
"<doc_customizing_html5_shell>`."
msgstr ""
"El més probable és que puguis. En primer lloc, heu d'incloure la vostra "
"biblioteca a la pàgina. Podeu personalitzar la :ref:`Head Include "
"<doc_javascript_export_options>` durant l'exportació (vegeu més avall), o "
"fins i tot :ref:`escriure la vostra pròpia plantilla "
"<doc_customizing_html5_shell>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:144
msgid ""
"In the example below, we customize the ``Head Include`` to add an external "
"library (`axios <https://axios-http.com/>`__) from a content delivery "
"network, and a second ``<script>`` tag to define our own custom function:"
msgstr ""
"A l'exemple següent, personalitzem la ``Head Include`` per afegir una "
"biblioteca externa (`axios <https://axios-http.com/>`__) des d'una xarxa de "
"lliurament de contingut, i una segona etiqueta ``<script>`` per definir la "
"nostra pròpia funció personalitzada:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:159
msgid ""
"We can then access both the library and the function from Godot, like we did "
"in previous examples:"
msgstr ""
"A continuació, podem accedir tant a la biblioteca com a la funció des de "
"Godot, com vam fer en exemples anteriors:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:185
msgid "The eval interface"
msgstr "La interfície eval"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:187
msgid ""
"The ``eval`` method works similarly to the JavaScript function of the same "
"name. It takes a string as an argument and executes it as JavaScript code. "
"This allows interacting with the browser in ways not possible with script "
"languages integrated into Godot."
msgstr ""
"El mètode ``eval`` funciona de manera similar a la funció JavaScript del "
"mateix nom. Pren una cadena com a argument i l'executa com a codi "
"JavaScript. Això permet interactuar amb el navegador d'una manera que no és "
"possible amb els llenguatges de script integrats a Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:205
msgid ""
"The value of the last JavaScript statement is converted to a GDScript value "
"and returned by ``eval()`` under certain circumstances:"
msgstr ""
"El valor de l'última instrucció de JavaScript es converteix en un valor "
"GDScript i es retorna per ``eval()`` en determinades circumstàncies:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:208
msgid "JavaScript ``number`` is returned as :ref:`class_float`"
msgstr "El ``número`` de JavaScript es retorna com a :ref:`class_float`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:209
msgid "JavaScript ``boolean`` is returned as :ref:`class_bool`"
msgstr "JavaScript ``boolean`` es retorna com a :ref:`class_bool`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:210
msgid "JavaScript ``string`` is returned as :ref:`class_String`"
msgstr "La ``cadena`` de JavaScript es retorna com a :ref:`class_String`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:211
msgid ""
"JavaScript ``ArrayBuffer``, ``TypedArray``, and ``DataView`` are returned "
"as :ref:`PackedByteArray<class_PackedByteArray>`"
msgstr ""
"JavaScript ``ArrayBuffer``, ``TypedArray`` i ``DataView`` es retornen com "
"a :ref:`PackedByteArray<class_PackedByteArray>`"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:228
msgid "Any other JavaScript value is returned as ``null``."
msgstr "Qualsevol altre valor de JavaScript es retorna com a ``null``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:230
msgid ""
"HTML5 export templates may be :ref:`built <doc_compiling_for_web>` without "
"support for the singleton to improve security. With such templates, and on "
"platforms other than HTML5, calling ``JavaScriptBridge.eval`` will also "
"return ``null``. The availability of the singleton can be checked with the "
"``web`` :ref:`feature tag <doc_feature_tags>`:"
msgstr ""
"Les plantilles d'exportació HTML5 poden ser :ref:`construïdes "
"<doc_compiling_for_web>` sense suport per al singleton per millorar la "
"seguretat. Amb aquestes plantilles, i en plataformes diferents d'HTML5, "
"cridar a ``JavaScriptBridge.eval`` també retornarà ``null``. La "
"disponibilitat del singleton es pot comprovar amb l'etiqueta de funció "
"``web`` :ref:` <doc_feature_tags>`:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:261
msgid ""
"GDScript's multi-line strings, surrounded by 3 quotes ``\"\"\"`` as in "
"``my_func3()`` above, are useful to keep JavaScript code readable."
msgstr ""
"Les cadenes de diverses línies de GDScript, envoltades de 3 cometes "
"``\"\"\"`` com a ``my_func3()`` anterior, són útils per mantenir el codi "
"JavaScript llegible."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:264
msgid ""
"The ``eval`` method also accepts a second, optional Boolean argument, which "
"specifies whether to execute the code in the global execution context, "
"defaulting to ``false`` to prevent polluting the global namespace:"
msgstr ""
"El mètode ``eval`` també accepta un segon argument booleà opcional, que "
"especifica si s'ha d'executar el codi en el context d'execució global, per "
"defecte ``false`` per evitar contaminar l'espai de noms global:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:289
msgid "Downloading files"
msgstr "Baixada de fitxers"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/platform/web/javascript_bridge.rst:291
msgid ""
"Downloading files (e.g. a save game) from the Godot Web export to the user's "
"computer can be done by directly interacting with JavaScript, but given it "
"is a very common use case, Godot exposes this functionality to scripting via "
"a dedicated :ref:`JavaScriptBridge.download_buffer() "
"<class_JavaScriptBridge_method_download_buffer>` function which lets you "
"download any generated buffer."
msgstr ""
"La descàrrega de fitxers (per exemple, una partida desa) des de l'exportació "
"web de Godot a l'ordinador de l'usuari es pot fer interactuant directament "
"amb JavaScript, però donat que és un cas d'ús molt comú, Godot exposa "
"aquesta funcionalitat a l'escriptura mitjançant "
"un :ref:`JavaScriptBridge.download_buffer() "
"<class_JavaScriptBridge_method_download_buffer>` que us permeti descarregar "
"qualsevol funció que us permeti generar un buffer."

