#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_variant.rst:138
msgid ""
"Godot uses 64-bit integers and floats in Variant. Smaller integer and float "
"types such as ``int``, ``short`` and ``float`` are supported since they can "
"fit in the bigger type. Be aware that when a conversion is performed, using "
"the wrong type will result in potential precision loss."
msgstr ""
"Godot utilitza nombres enters de 64 bits i flotants a Variant. Els tipus "
"d'enters i flotants més petits com ara ``int``, ``short`` i ``float`` "
"s'admeten ja que poden cabre en el tipus més gran. Tingueu en compte que "
"quan es realitza una conversió, utilitzar el tipus incorrecte pot provocar "
"una pèrdua de precisió potencial."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_variant.rst:145
msgid ""
"Enums are supported by ``Godot.Variant`` since their underlying type is an "
"integer type which are all compatible. However, implicit conversions don't "
"exist, enums must be manually converted to their underlying integer type "
"before they can converted to/from ``Godot.Variant`` or use the generic "
"``Variant.As<T>`` and ``Variant.From<T>`` methods to convert them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_variant.rst:162
msgid "Using Variant in a generic context"
msgstr "Ús de Variant en un context genèric"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_variant.rst:164
msgid ""
"When using generics, you may be interested in restricting the generic ``T`` "
"type to be only one of the Variant-compatible types. This can be achieved "
"using the ``[MustBeVariant]`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"Quan utilitzeu genèrics, potser us interessa restringir el tipus genèric "
"``T`` perquè sigui només un dels tipus compatibles amb Variant. Això es pot "
"aconseguir mitjançant l'atribut ``[MustBeVariant]``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_variant.rst:175
msgid ""
"Combined with the generic ``Variant.From<T>`` allows you to obtain an "
"instance of ``Godot.Variant`` from an instance of a generic ``T`` type. Then "
"it can be used in any API that only supports the ``Godot.Variant`` struct."
msgstr ""
"Combinat amb el genèric ``Variant.From<T>`` us permet obtenir una instància "
"de ``Godot.Variant`` a partir d'una instància d'un tipus genèric ``T``. "
"Aleshores es pot utilitzar en qualsevol API que només admeti l'estructura "
"``Godot.Variant``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_variant.rst:192
msgid ""
"In order to invoke a method with a generic parameter annotated with the "
"``[MustBeVariant]`` attribute, the value must be a Variant-compatible type "
"or a generic ``T`` type annotated with the ``[MustBeVariant]`` attribute as "
"well."
msgstr ""
"Per invocar un mètode amb un paràmetre genèric anotat amb l'atribut "
"``[MustBeVariant]``, el valor ha de ser un tipus compatible amb variants o "
"un tipus genèric ``T`` anotat també amb l'atribut ``[MustBeVariant]``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:4
msgid "C# signals"
msgstr "Senyals C#"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:6
msgid ""
"For a detailed explanation of signals in general, see the :ref:`doc_signals` "
"section in the step by step tutorial."
msgstr ""
"Per obtenir una explicació detallada dels senyals en general, consulteu la "
"secció :ref:`doc_signals` del tutorial pas a pas."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:9
msgid ""
"Signals are implemented using C# events, the idiomatic way to "
"represent :ref:`the observer pattern<doc_key_concepts_signals>` in C#. This "
"is the recommended way to use signals in C# and the focus of this page."
msgstr ""
"Els senyals s'implementen mitjançant esdeveniments C#, la manera idiomàtica "
"de representar :ref:`el patró d'observador<doc_key_concepts_signals>` en C#. "
"Aquesta és la manera recomanada d'utilitzar els senyals en C# i el focus "
"d'aquesta pàgina."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:13
msgid ""
"In some cases it's necessary to use the "
"older :ref:`Connect()<class_object_method_connect>` "
"and :ref:`Disconnect()<class_object_method_disconnect>` APIs. "
"See :ref:`using_connect_and_disconnect` for more details."
msgstr ""
"En alguns casos, és necessari utilitzar les API més "
"antigues :ref:`Connect()<class_object_method_connect>` "
"i :ref:`Disconnect()<class_object_method_disconnect>`. "
"Vegeu :ref:`using_connect_and_disconnect` per a més detalls."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:18
msgid ""
"If you encounter a ``System.ObjectDisposedException`` while handling a "
"signal, you might be missing a signal disconnection. "
"See :ref:`disconnecting_automatically_when_the_receiver_is_freed` for more "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Si trobeu una ``System.ObjectDisposedException`` mentre manegeu un senyal, "
"és possible que us perdeu una desconnexió del senyal. "
"Vegeu :ref:`disconnecting_automatically_when_the_receiver_is_freed` per a "
"més detalls."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:23
msgid "Signals as C# events"
msgstr "Senyals com a esdeveniments C#"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:25
msgid ""
"To provide more type-safety, Godot signals are also all available through "
"`events <https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/events-overview>`_. "
"You can handle these events, as any other event, with the ``+=`` and ``-=`` "
"operators."
msgstr ""
"Per oferir més seguretat de tipus, els senyals Godot també estan disponibles "
"a través dels `esdeveniments <https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/"
"csharp/events-overview>`_. Podeu gestionar aquests esdeveniments, com "
"qualsevol altre esdeveniment, amb els operadors ``+=`` i ``-=``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:33
msgid ""
"In addition, you can always access signal names associated with a node type "
"through its nested ``SignalName`` class. This is useful when, for example, "
"you want to await on a signal (see :ref:`doc_c_sharp_differences_await`)."
msgstr ""
"A més, sempre podeu accedir als noms de senyal associats a un tipus de node "
"mitjançant la seva classe imbricada ``SignalName``. Això és útil quan, per "
"exemple, voleu esperar un senyal "
"(vegeu :ref:`doc_c_sharp_differences_await`)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:41
msgid "Custom signals as C# events"
msgstr "Senyals personalitzats com a esdeveniments C#"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:43
msgid ""
"To declare a custom event in your C# script, use the ``[Signal]`` attribute "
"on a public delegate type. Note that the name of this delegate needs to end "
"with ``EventHandler``."
msgstr ""
"Per declarar un esdeveniment personalitzat al vostre script C#, utilitzeu "
"l'atribut ``[Signal]`` en un tipus de delegat públic. Tingueu en compte que "
"el nom d'aquest delegat ha d'acabar amb ``EventHandler``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:54
msgid ""
"Once this is done, Godot will create the appropriate events automatically "
"behind the scenes. You can then use said events as you'd do for any other "
"Godot signal. Note that events are named using your delegate's name minus "
"the final ``EventHandler`` part."
msgstr ""
"Un cop fet això, Godot crearà automàticament els esdeveniments adequats "
"entre bastidors. A continuació, podeu utilitzar aquests esdeveniments com ho "
"faries per a qualsevol altre senyal de Godot. Tingueu en compte que els "
"esdeveniments s'anomenen amb el nom del vostre delegat menys la part final "
"d'\"EventHandler\"."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:73
msgid ""
"If you want to connect to these signals in the editor, you will need to "
"(re)build the project to see them appear."
msgstr ""
"Si voleu connectar-vos a aquests senyals a l'editor, haureu de (re)construir "
"el projecte per veure'ls aparèixer."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:76
msgid ""
"You can click the **Build** button in the upper-right corner of the editor "
"to do so."
msgstr ""
"Per fer-ho, podeu fer clic al botó **Construeix** a l'extrem superior dret "
"de l'editor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:79
msgid "Signal emission"
msgstr "Senyals"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:81
msgid ""
"To emit signals, use the ``EmitSignal`` method. Note that, as for signals "
"defined by the engine, your custom signal names are listed under the nested "
"``SignalName`` class."
msgstr ""
"Per emetre senyals, utilitzeu el mètode ``EmitSignal``. Tingueu en compte "
"que, pel que fa als senyals definits pel motor, els vostres noms de senyal "
"personalitzats es mostren a la classe ``SignalName`` imbricada."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:92
msgid ""
"In contrast with other C# events, you cannot use ``Invoke`` to raise events "
"tied to Godot signals."
msgstr ""
"A diferència d'altres esdeveniments C#, no podeu utilitzar ``Invoke`` per "
"generar esdeveniments vinculats als senyals Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:94
msgid ""
"Signals support arguments of any :ref:`Variant-compatible type "
"<c_sharp_variant_compatible_types>`."
msgstr ""
"Els senyals admeten arguments de qualsevol :ref:`Tipus compatible amb "
"variants <c_sharp_variant_compatible_types>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:96
msgid ""
"Consequently, any ``Node`` or ``RefCounted`` will be compatible "
"automatically, but custom data objects will need to inherit from "
"``GodotObject`` or one of its subclasses."
msgstr ""
"En conseqüència, qualsevol ``Node`` o ``RefCounted`` serà compatible "
"automàticament, però els objectes de dades personalitzats hauran d'heretar "
"de ``GodotObject`` o d'una de les seves subclasses."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:110
msgid "Bound values"
msgstr "Valors lligats"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:112
msgid ""
"Sometimes you'll want to bind values to a signal when the connection is "
"established, rather than (or in addition to) when the signal is emitted. To "
"do so, you can use an anonymous function like in the following example."
msgstr ""
"De vegades, voldreu enllaçar valors a un senyal quan s'estableixi la "
"connexió, en lloc de (o a més) quan s'emet el senyal. Per fer-ho, podeu "
"utilitzar una funció anònima com a l'exemple següent."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:116
msgid ""
"Here, the :ref:`Button.Pressed <class_BaseButton_signal_pressed>` signal "
"does not take any argument. But we want to use the same ``ModifyValue`` for "
"both the \"plus\" and \"minus\" buttons. So we bind the modifier value at "
"the time we're connecting the signals."
msgstr ""
"Aquí, el senyal :ref:`Button.Pressed <class_BaseButton_signal_pressed>` no "
"accepta cap argument. Però volem utilitzar el mateix ``ModifyValue`` tant "
"per als botons \"més\" com \"menys\". Així que enllacem el valor del "
"modificador en el moment que connectem els senyals."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:139
msgid "Signal creation at runtime"
msgstr "Creació del senyal en temps d'execució"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:141
msgid ""
"Finally, you can create custom signals directly while your game is running. "
"Use the ``AddUserSignal`` method for that. Be aware that it should be "
"executed before any use of said signals (either connecting to them or "
"emitting them). Also, note that signals created this way won't be visible "
"through the ``SignalName`` nested class."
msgstr ""
"Finalment, podeu crear senyals personalitzats directament mentre el vostre "
"joc s'executa. Utilitzeu el mètode ``AddUserSignal`` per a això. Tingueu en "
"compte que s'ha d'executar abans de qualsevol ús d'aquests senyals (ja sigui "
"per connectar-hi o emetre'ls). A més, tingueu en compte que els senyals "
"creats d'aquesta manera no seran visibles a través de la classe imbricada "
"``SignalName``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:157
msgid "Using Connect and Disconnect"
msgstr "Ús de Connect i Disconnect"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:159
msgid ""
"In general, it isn't recommended to "
"use :ref:`Connect()<class_object_method_connect>` "
"and :ref:`Disconnect()<class_object_method_disconnect>`. These APIs don't "
"provide as much type safety as the events. However, they're necessary "
"for :ref:`connecting to signals defined by GDScript "
"<connecting_to_signals_cross_language>` and "
"passing :ref:`ConnectFlags<enum_Object_ConnectFlags>`."
msgstr ""
"En general, no es recomana "
"utilitzar :ref:`Connect()<class_object_method_connect>` "
"i :ref:`Disconnect()<class_object_method_disconnect>`. Aquestes API no "
"proporcionen tanta seguretat com els esdeveniments. Tanmateix, són "
"necessaris per :ref:`connectar-se als senyals definits per GDScript "
"<connecting_to_signals_cross_language>` i "
"passar :ref:`ConnectFlags<enum_Object_ConnectFlags>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:166
msgid ""
"In the following example, pressing the button for the first time prints "
"``Greetings!``. ``OneShot`` disconnects the signal, so pressing the button "
"again does nothing."
msgstr ""
"A l'exemple següent, en prémer el botó per primera vegada s'imprimeix "
"``Salutacions!``. ``OneShot`` desconnecta el senyal, de manera que tornar a "
"prémer el botó no fa res."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:186
msgid "Disconnecting automatically when the receiver is freed"
msgstr "Es desconnecta automàticament quan s'allibera el receptor"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:188
msgid ""
"Normally, when any ``GodotObject`` is freed (such as any ``Node``), Godot "
"automatically disconnects all connections associated with that object. This "
"happens for both signal emitters and signal receivers."
msgstr ""
"Normalment, quan s'allibera qualsevol ``GodotObject`` (com qualsevol "
"``Node``), Godot desconnecta automàticament totes les connexions associades "
"a aquest objecte. Això passa tant per als emissors de senyal com per als "
"receptors de senyal."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:192
msgid ""
"For example, a node with this code will print \"Hello!\" when the button is "
"pressed, then free itself. Freeing the node disconnects the signal, so "
"pressing the button again doesn't do anything:"
msgstr ""
"Per exemple, un node amb aquest codi imprimirà \"Hola!\" quan es prem el "
"botó, allibera'l. Alliberar el node desconnecta el senyal, de manera que "
"tornar a prémer el botó no fa res:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:210
msgid ""
"When a signal receiver is freed while the signal emitter is still alive, in "
"some cases automatic disconnection won't happen:"
msgstr ""
"Quan s'allibera un receptor de senyal mentre l'emissor de senyal encara està "
"viu, en alguns casos no es produirà la desconnexió automàtica:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:213
msgid ""
"The signal is connected to a lambda expression that captures a variable."
msgstr ""
"El senyal està connectat a una expressió lambda que captura una variable."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:214
msgid "The signal is a custom signal."
msgstr "El senyal és un senyal personalitzat."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:216
msgid ""
"The following sections explain these cases in more detail and include "
"suggestions for how to disconnect manually."
msgstr ""
"Les seccions següents expliquen aquests casos amb més detall i inclouen "
"suggeriments sobre com desconnectar-se manualment."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:221
msgid ""
"Automatic disconnection is totally reliable if a signal emitter is freed "
"before any of its receivers are freed. With a project style that prefers "
"this pattern, the above limits may not be a concern."
msgstr ""
"La desconnexió automàtica és totalment fiable si un emissor de senyal "
"s'allibera abans que qualsevol dels seus receptors s'alliberi. Amb un estil "
"de projecte que prefereix aquest patró, els límits anteriors poden no ser "
"una preocupació."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:226
msgid ""
"No automatic disconnection: a lambda expression that captures a variable"
msgstr ""
"Sense desconnexió automàtica: una expressió lambda que captura una variable"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:228
msgid ""
"If you connect to a lambda expression that captures variables, Godot can't "
"tell that the lambda is associated with the instance that created it. This "
"causes this example to have potentially unexpected behavior:"
msgstr ""
"Si us connecteu a una expressió lambda que captura variables, Godot no pot "
"dir que la lambda està associada a la instància que l'ha creat. Això fa que "
"aquest exemple tingui un comportament potencialment inesperat:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:255
msgid ""
"On tick 4, the lambda expression tries to access the ``Name`` property of "
"the node, but the node has already been freed. This causes the exception."
msgstr ""
"A la marca 4, l'expressió lambda intenta accedir a la propietat ``Name`` del "
"node, però el node ja s'ha alliberat. Això provoca l'excepció."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:258
msgid ""
"To disconnect, keep a reference to the delegate created by the lambda "
"expression and pass that to ``-=``. For example, this node connects and "
"disconnects using the ``_EnterTree`` and ``_ExitTree`` lifecycle methods:"
msgstr ""
"Per desconnectar, manteniu una referència al delegat creat per l'expressió "
"lambda i passeu-la a ``-=``. Per exemple, aquest node es connecta i es "
"desconnecta mitjançant els mètodes de cicle de vida ``_EnterTree`` i "
"``_ExitTree``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:290
msgid ""
"In this example, ``Free`` causes the node to leave the tree, which calls "
"``_ExitTree``. ``_ExitTree`` disconnects the signal, so ``_tick`` is never "
"called again."
msgstr ""
"En aquest exemple, ``Free`` fa que el node surti de l'arbre, que crida "
"``_ExitTree``. ``_ExitTree`` desconnecta el senyal, de manera que ``_tick`` "
"no es torna a cridar mai més."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:294
msgid ""
"The lifecycle methods to use depend on what the node does. Another option is "
"to connect to signals in ``_Ready`` and disconnect in ``Dispose``."
msgstr ""
"Els mètodes de cicle de vida a utilitzar depenen del que fa el node. Una "
"altra opció és connectar-se als senyals a ``_Ready`` i desconnectar a "
"``Dispose``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:299
msgid ""
"Godot uses `Delegate.Target <https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/"
"system.delegate.target>`_ to determine what instance a delegate is "
"associated with. When a lambda expression doesn't capture a variable, the "
"generated delegate's ``Target`` is the instance that created the delegate. "
"When a variable is captured, the ``Target`` instead points at a generated "
"type that stores the captured variable. This is what breaks the association. "
"If you want to see if a delegate will be automatically cleaned up, try "
"checking its ``Target``."
msgstr ""
"Godot utilitza `Delegate.Target <https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/"
"api/system.delegate.target>`_ per determinar a quina instància està associat "
"un delegat. Quan una expressió lambda no captura una variable, el ``Target`` "
"del delegat generat és la instància que ha creat el delegat. Quan es captura "
"una variable, ``Target`` apunta a un tipus generat que emmagatzema la "
"variable capturada. Això és el que trenca l'associació. Si voleu veure si un "
"delegat es netejarà automàticament, proveu de comprovar el seu ``Target``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:307
msgid ""
"``Callable.From`` doesn't affect the ``Delegate.Target``, so connecting a "
"lambda that captures variables using ``Connect`` doesn't work any better "
"than ``+=``."
msgstr ""
"``Callable.From`` no afecta el ``Delegate.Target``, de manera que connectar "
"una lambda que captura variables amb ``Connect`` no funciona millor que "
"``+=``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:312
msgid "No automatic disconnection: a custom signal"
msgstr "Sense desconnexió automàtica: un senyal personalitzat"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:314
msgid ""
"Connecting to a custom signal using ``+=`` doesn't disconnect automatically "
"when the receiving node is freed."
msgstr ""
"La connexió a un senyal personalitzat amb ``+=`` no es desconnecta "
"automàticament quan s'allibera el node receptor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:317
msgid "To disconnect, use ``-=`` at an appropriate time. For example:"
msgstr "Per desconnectar, utilitzeu ``-=`` en el moment adequat. Per exemple:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_signals.rst:334
msgid ""
"Another solution is to use ``Connect``, which does disconnect automatically "
"with custom signals:"
msgstr ""
"Una altra solució és utilitzar ``Connect``, que es desconnecta "
"automàticament amb senyals personalitzats:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:4
msgid "C# exported properties"
msgstr "Propietats exportades de C#"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:6
msgid ""
"In Godot, class members can be exported. This means their value gets saved "
"along with the resource (such as the :ref:`scene <class_PackedScene>`) "
"they're attached to. They will also be available for editing in the property "
"editor. Exporting is done by using the ``[Export]`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"A Godot, els membres de la classe es poden exportar. Això vol dir que el seu "
"valor es desa juntament amb el recurs (com ara la :ref:`scene "
"<class_PackedScene>`) al qual estan connectats. També estaran disponibles "
"per editar-los a l'editor de propietats. L'exportació es fa mitjançant "
"l'atribut ``[Export]``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:21
msgid ""
"In that example the value ``5`` will be saved, and after building the "
"current project it will be visible in the property editor."
msgstr ""
"En aquest exemple es desarà el valor ``5`` i després de construir el "
"projecte actual serà visible a l'editor de propietats."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:24
msgid ""
"One of the fundamental benefits of exporting member variables is to have "
"them visible and editable in the editor. This way, artists and game "
"designers can modify values that later influence how the program runs. For "
"this, a special export syntax is provided."
msgstr ""
"Un dels avantatges fonamentals d'exportar variables membres és tenir-les "
"visibles i editables a l'editor. D'aquesta manera, els artistes i "
"dissenyadors de jocs poden modificar valors que posteriorment influeixen en "
"el funcionament del programa. Per a això, es proporciona una sintaxi "
"d'exportació especial."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:29
msgid ""
"Exporting can only be done with :ref:`c_sharp_variant_compatible_types`."
msgstr ""
"L'exportació només es pot fer amb :ref:`c_sharp_variant_compatible_types`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:33
msgid ""
"Exporting properties can also be done in GDScript, for information on that "
"see :ref:`doc_gdscript_exports`."
msgstr ""
"L'exportació de propietats també es pot fer a GDScript, per obtenir "
"informació sobre això, vegeu :ref:`doc_gdscript_exports`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:39
msgid ""
"Exporting works with fields and properties. They can have any access "
"modifier."
msgstr ""
"Exportar obres amb camps i propietats. Poden tenir qualsevol modificador "
"d'accés."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:49
msgid ""
"Exported members can specify a default value; otherwise, the `default value "
"of the type <https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/language-"
"reference/builtin-types/default-values>`_ is used instead."
msgstr ""
"Els membres exportats poden especificar un valor predeterminat; en cas "
"contrari, s'utilitza el `valor per defecte del tipus <https://"
"learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/csharp/language-reference/builtin-types/"
"default-values>`_."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:51
msgid ""
"An ``int`` like ``Number`` defaults to ``0``. ``Text`` defaults to null "
"because ``string`` is a reference type."
msgstr ""
"Un ``int`` com ``Number`` per defecte és ``0``. ``Text`` és nul per defecte "
"perquè ``cadena`` és un tipus de referència."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:62
msgid "Default values can be specified for fields and properties."
msgstr "Es poden especificar valors per defecte per a camps i propietats."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:72
msgid ""
"Properties with a backing field use the default value of the backing field."
msgstr ""
"Les propietats amb un camp de suport utilitzen el valor predeterminat del "
"camp de suport."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:87
msgid ""
"A property's ``get`` is not actually executed to determine the default "
"value. Instead, Godot analyzes the C# source code. This works fine for most "
"cases, such as the examples on this page. However, some properties are too "
"complex for the analyzer to understand."
msgstr ""
"El ``get`` d'una propietat no s'executa realment per determinar el valor "
"predeterminat. En canvi, Godot analitza el codi font C#. Això funciona bé en "
"la majoria dels casos, com els exemples d'aquesta pàgina. Tanmateix, algunes "
"propietats són massa complexes perquè l'analitzador les entengui."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:92
msgid ""
"For example, the following property attempts to use math to display the "
"default value as ``5`` in the property editor, but it doesn't work:"
msgstr ""
"Per exemple, la propietat següent intenta utilitzar les matemàtiques per "
"mostrar el valor predeterminat com a ``5`` a l'editor de propietats, però no "
"funciona:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:106
msgid ""
"The analyzer doesn't understand this code and falls back to the default "
"value for ``int``, ``0``. However, when running the scene or inspecting a "
"node with an attached tool script, ``_number`` will be ``2``, and "
"``NumberWithBackingField`` will return ``5``. This difference may cause "
"confusing behavior. To avoid this, don't use complex properties. "
"Alternatively, if the default value can be explicitly specified, it can be "
"overridden with the :ref:`_PropertyCanRevert() "
"<class_Object_private_method__property_can_revert>` "
"and :ref:`_PropertyGetRevert() "
"<class_Object_private_method__property_get_revert>` methods."
msgstr ""
"L'analitzador no entén aquest codi i torna al valor predeterminat de "
"``int``, ``0``. Tanmateix, quan executeu l'escena o inspeccioneu un node amb "
"un script d'eina adjunt, ``_number`` serà ``2`` i ``NumberWithBackingField`` "
"retornarà ``5``. Aquesta diferència pot provocar un comportament confús. Per "
"evitar-ho, no utilitzeu propietats complexes. Alternativament, si el valor "
"predeterminat es pot especificar explícitament, es pot substituir amb els "
"mètodes :ref:`_PropertyCanRevert() "
"<class_Object_private_method__property_can_revert>` "
"i :ref:`_PropertyGetRevert() "
"<class_Object_private_method__property_get_revert>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:115
msgid ""
"Any type of ``Resource`` or ``Node`` can be exported. The property editor "
"shows a user-friendly assignment dialog for these types. This can be used "
"instead of ``GD.Load`` and ``GetNode``. See :ref:`Nodes and Resources "
"<doc_c_sharp_exports_nodes>`."
msgstr ""
"Es pot exportar qualsevol tipus de ``Recurs`` o ``Node``. L'editor de "
"propietats mostra un diàleg d'assignació fàcil d'utilitzar per a aquests "
"tipus. Això es pot utilitzar en lloc de ``GD.Load`` i ``GetNode``. "
"Vegeu :ref:`Nodes i recursos <doc_c_sharp_exports_nodes>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:130
msgid ""
"It is possible to group your exported properties inside the Inspector with "
"the ``[ExportGroup]`` attribute. Every exported property after this "
"attribute will be added to the group. Start a new group or use "
"``[ExportGroup(\"\")]`` to break out."
msgstr ""
"És possible agrupar les propietats exportades dins de l'Inspector amb "
"l'atribut ``[ExportGroup]``. Totes les propietats exportades després "
"d'aquest atribut s'afegiran al grup. Inicia un grup nou o utilitza "
"``[ExportGroup(\"\")]`` per sortir."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:140
msgid ""
"The second argument of the attribute can be used to only group properties "
"with the specified prefix."
msgstr ""
"El segon argument de l'atribut només es pot utilitzar per agrupar propietats "
"amb el prefix especificat."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:142
msgid ""
"Groups cannot be nested, use ``[ExportSubgroup]`` to create subgroups within "
"a group."
msgstr ""
"Els grups no es poden niar, utilitzeu ``[ExportSubgroup]`` per crear "
"subgrups dins d'un grup."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:152
msgid ""
"You can also change the name of your main category, or create additional "
"categories in the property list with the ``[ExportCategory]`` attribute."
msgstr ""
"També podeu canviar el nom de la vostra categoria principal o crear "
"categories addicionals a la llista de propietats amb l'atribut "
"``[ExportCategory]``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:169
msgid ""
"The list of properties is organized based on the class inheritance, and new "
"categories break that expectation. Use them carefully, especially when "
"creating projects for public use."
msgstr ""
"La llista de propietats s'organitza en funció de l'herència de classe i les "
"noves categories trenquen aquesta expectativa. Utilitzeu-los amb cura, "
"sobretot quan creeu projectes d'ús públic."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:175
msgid "Property hints can be used to export strings as paths"
msgstr ""
"Els suggeriments de propietat es poden utilitzar per exportar cadenes com a "
"camins"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:177
msgid "String as a path to a file."
msgstr "Cadena com a camí a un fitxer."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:184
msgid "String as a path to a directory."
msgstr "Cadena com a camí d'accés a un directori."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:191
msgid "String as a path to a file, custom filter provided as hint."
msgstr ""
"Cadena com a camí d'accés a un fitxer, filtre personalitzat proporcionat com "
"a pista."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:201
msgid "String as a path to a PNG file in the global filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Cadena com a camí d'accés a un fitxer PNG al sistema de fitxers global."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:208
msgid "String as a path to a directory in the global filesystem."
msgstr ""
"Cadena com a camí d'accés a un directori del sistema de fitxers global."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:215
msgid ""
"The multiline annotation tells the editor to show a large input field for "
"editing over multiple lines."
msgstr ""
"L'anotació multilínia indica a l'editor que mostri un camp d'entrada gran "
"per editar-lo en diverses línies."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:226
msgid ""
"Using the range property hint allows you to limit what can be input as a "
"value using the editor."
msgstr ""
"L'ús de la pista de propietat range us permet limitar el que es pot "
"introduir com a valor mitjançant l'editor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:250
msgid ""
"If you add the hints \"or_greater\" and/or \"or_less\" you can go above or "
"below the limits when adjusting the value by typing it instead of using the "
"slider."
msgstr ""
"Si afegiu els suggeriments \"or_greater\" i/o \"or_less\", podeu anar per "
"sobre o per sota dels límits quan ajusteu el valor escrivint-lo en lloc "
"d'utilitzar el control lliscant."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:262
msgid ""
"Display a visual representation of "
"the :ref:`ease<class_@GlobalScope_method_ease>` function when editing."
msgstr ""
"Mostra una representació visual de la "
"funció :ref:`ease<class_@GlobalScope_method_ease>` en editar."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:271
msgid "Export with suffix hint"
msgstr "Exporta amb una pista de sufix"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:273
msgid ""
"Display a unit hint suffix for exported variables. Works with numeric types, "
"such as floats or vectors:"
msgstr ""
"Mostra un sufix d'indicació d'unitat per a les variables exportades. "
"Funciona amb tipus numèrics, com ara flotants o vectors:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:283
msgid ""
"In the above example, ``\\u00b2`` is used to write the \"squared\" character "
"(``²``)."
msgstr ""
"A l'exemple anterior, ``\\u00b2`` s'utilitza per escriure el caràcter "
"\"quadrat\" (``²``)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:296
msgid "Color given as red-green-blue value (alpha will always be 1)."
msgstr "Color donat com a valor vermell-verd-blau (alfa sempre serà 1)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:308
msgid "Nodes can also be directly exported without having to use NodePaths."
msgstr ""
"Els nodes també es poden exportar directament sense haver d'utilitzar "
"NodePaths."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:315
msgid ""
"A specific type of node can also be directly exported. The list of nodes "
"shown after pressing \"Assign\" in the inspector is filtered to the "
"specified type, and only a correct node can be assigned."
msgstr ""
"També es pot exportar directament un tipus de node específic. La llista de "
"nodes que es mostra després de prémer \"Assigna\" a l'inspector es filtra al "
"tipus especificat i només es pot assignar un node correcte."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:324
msgid ""
"Custom node classes can also be exported directly. The filtering behavior "
"depends on whether the custom class is a :ref:`global class "
"<doc_c_sharp_global_classes>`."
msgstr ""
"Les classes de nodes personalitzades també es poden exportar directament. El "
"comportament del filtratge depèn de si la classe personalitzada és "
"una :ref:`classe global <doc_c_sharp_global_classes>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:351
msgid ""
"Opening the inspector dropdown may result in an extremely long list of "
"possible classes to create, however. Therefore, if you specify a type "
"derived from Resource such as:"
msgstr ""
"Tanmateix, l'obertura del menú desplegable de l'inspector pot resultar en "
"una llista extremadament llarga de possibles classes per crear. Per tant, si "
"especifiqueu un tipus derivat de Resource com ara:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:360
msgid ""
"The drop-down menu will be limited to AnimationNode and all its derived "
"classes. Custom resource classes can also be used, "
"see :ref:`doc_c_sharp_global_classes`."
msgstr ""
"El menú desplegable estarà limitat a AnimationNode i totes les seves classes "
"derivades. També es poden utilitzar classes de recursos personalitzades, "
"vegeu :ref:`doc_c_sharp_global_classes`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:364
msgid ""
"It must be noted that even if the script is not being run while in the "
"editor, the exported properties are still editable. This can be used in "
"conjunction with a :ref:`script in \"tool\" mode <doc_gdscript_tool_mode>`."
msgstr ""
"Cal tenir en compte que, fins i tot si l'script no s'està executant a "
"l'editor, les propietats exportades encara es poden editar. Això es pot "
"utilitzar juntament amb un script :ref:` en mode \"eina\" "
"<doc_gdscript_tool_mode>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:371
msgid ""
"Members whose type is an enum with the ``[Flags]`` attribute can be exported "
"and their values are limited to the members of the enum type. The editor "
"will create a widget in the Inspector, allowing to select none, one, or "
"multiple of the enum members. The value will be stored as an integer."
msgstr ""
"Els membres el tipus dels quals és una enumeració amb l'atribut ``[Flags]`` "
"es poden exportar i els seus valors es limiten als membres del tipus "
"enumeració. L'editor crearà un giny a l'Inspector, que permetrà seleccionar "
"cap, un o diversos dels membres enumerats. El valor s'emmagatzemarà com un "
"nombre enter."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:376
msgid ""
"A flags enum uses powers of 2 for the values of the enum members. Members "
"that combine multiple flags using logical OR (``|``) are also possible."
msgstr ""
"Una enumeració flags utilitza poders de 2 per als valors dels membres de la "
"enumeració. També són possibles els membres que combinen diversos indicadors "
"mitjançant l'OR lògic (``|``)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:395
msgid ""
"Integers used as bit flags can store multiple ``true``/``false`` (boolean) "
"values in one property. By using the ``Flags`` property hint, any of the "
"given flags can be set from the editor."
msgstr ""
"Els enters utilitzats com a indicadors de bits poden emmagatzemar diversos "
"valors ``true``/``fals`` (booleans) en una propietat. Mitjançant l'ús de la "
"pista de propietat ``Flags``, qualsevol dels indicadors donats es pot "
"establir des de l'editor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:404
msgid ""
"You must provide a string description for each flag. In this example, "
"``Fire`` has value 1, ``Water`` has value 2, ``Earth`` has value 4 and "
"``Wind`` corresponds to value 8. Usually, constants should be defined "
"accordingly (e.g. ``private const int ElementWind = 8`` and so on)."
msgstr ""
"Heu de proporcionar una descripció de cadena per a cada marca. En aquest "
"exemple, ``Foc`` té el valor 1, ``Aigua`` té el valor 2, ``Terra`` té el "
"valor 4 i ``Vent`` correspon al valor 8. Normalment, les constants s'han de "
"definir en conseqüència (per exemple, ``private const int ElementWind = 8`` "
"i així successivament)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:425
msgid ""
"Export annotations are also provided for the physics and render layers "
"defined in the project settings."
msgstr ""
"També es proporcionen anotacions d'exportació per a les capes físiques i de "
"renderització definides a la configuració del projecte."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:444
msgid ""
"Members whose type is an enum can be exported and their values are limited "
"to the members of the enum type. The editor will create a widget in the "
"Inspector, enumerating the following as \"Thing 1\", \"Thing 2\", \"Another "
"Thing\". The value will be stored as an integer."
msgstr ""
"Els membres el tipus dels quals és una enumeració es poden exportar i els "
"seus valors es limiten als membres del tipus enumeració. L'editor crearà un "
"widget a l'Inspector, enumerant el següent com a \"Cosa 1\", \"Cosa 2\", "
"\"Una altra cosa\". El valor s'emmagatzemarà com un nombre enter."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:460
msgid ""
"Integer and string members can also be limited to a specific list of values "
"using the ``[Export]`` annotation with the ``PropertyHint.Enum`` hint. The "
"editor will create a widget in the Inspector, enumerating the following as "
"Warrior, Magician, Thief. The value will be stored as an integer, "
"corresponding to the index of the selected option (i.e. ``0``, ``1``, or "
"``2``)."
msgstr ""
"Els membres enters i de cadena també es poden limitar a una llista "
"específica de valors mitjançant l'anotació ``[Export]`` amb la pista "
"``PropertyHint.Enum``. L'editor crearà un giny a l'Inspector, enumerant el "
"següent com a Guerrer, Mag, Lladre. El valor s'emmagatzemarà com un nombre "
"enter, corresponent a l'índex de l'opció seleccionada (és a dir, ``0``, "
"``1`` o ``2``)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:478
msgid "If the type is ``string``, the value will be stored as a string."
msgstr "Si el tipus és ``cadena``, el valor s'emmagatzemarà com una cadena."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:494
msgid "Exporting inspector buttons with ``[ExportToolButton]``"
msgstr "S'estan exportant botons d'inspector amb ``[ExportToolButton]``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:496
msgid ""
"If you want to create a clickable button in the inspector, you can use the "
"``[ExportToolButton]`` attribute.  This exports a Callable property or field "
"as a clickable button. Since this runs in the editor, usage of "
"the :ref:`[Tool] <doc_running_code_in_the_editor>` attribute is required. "
"When the button is pressed, the callable is called:"
msgstr ""
"Si voleu crear un botó clicable a l'inspector, podeu utilitzar l'atribut "
"``[ExportToolButton]``.  Això exporta una propietat o un camp que es pot "
"cridar com a botó en què es pot fer clic. Com que això s'executa a l'editor, "
"cal utilitzar l'atribut :ref:`[Tool] <doc_running_code_in_the_editor>`. Quan "
"es prem el botó, es crida l'anomenat:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:516
msgid ""
"You can also set an icon for the button with a second argument. If "
"specified, an icon will be fetched via :ref:`GetThemeIcon() "
"<class_Control_method_get_theme_icon>`, from the ``\"EditorIcons\"`` theme "
"type."
msgstr ""
"També podeu establir una icona per al botó amb un segon argument. Si "
"s'especifica, s'obtindrà una icona mitjançant :ref:`GetThemeIcon() "
"<class_Control_method_get_theme_icon>`, del tipus de tema "
"``\"EditorIcons\"``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:526
msgid "Exporting collections"
msgstr "Exportació de col·leccions"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:528
msgid ""
"As explained in the :ref:`C# Variant <doc_c_sharp_variant>` documentation, "
"only certain C# arrays and the collection types defined in the "
"``Godot.Collections`` namespace are Variant-compatible, therefore, only "
"those types can be exported."
msgstr ""
"Tal com s'explica a la documentació :ref:`C# Variant <doc_c_sharp_variant>`, "
"només algunes matrius C# i els tipus de col·lecció definits a l'espai de "
"noms ``Godot.Collections`` són compatibles amb les variants, per tant, només "
"aquests tipus es poden exportar."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:533
msgid "Exporting Godot arrays"
msgstr "Exportació de matrius del Godot"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:540
msgid ""
"Using the generic ``Godot.Collections.Array<T>`` allows specifying the type "
"of the array elements, which will be used as a hint for the editor. The "
"Inspector will restrict the elements to the specified type."
msgstr ""
"L'ús del genèric ``Godot.Collections.Array<T>`` permet especificar el tipus "
"d'elements de la matriu, que s'utilitzaran com a pista per a l'editor. "
"L'inspector restringirà els elements al tipus especificat."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:549
msgid ""
"The default value of Godot arrays is null. A different default can be "
"specified:"
msgstr ""
"El valor per defecte de les matrius Godot és nul. Es pot especificar un "
"valor predeterminat diferent:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:573
msgid "Exporting Godot dictionaries"
msgstr "Exportació de diccionaris del Godot"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:580
msgid ""
"Using the generic ``Godot.Collections.Dictionary<TKey, TValue>`` allows "
"specifying the types of the key and value elements of the dictionary."
msgstr ""
"L'ús del genèric ``Godot.Collections.Dictionary<TKey, TValue>`` permet "
"especificar els tipus d'elements clau i valor del diccionari."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:588
msgid ""
"The default value of Godot dictionaries is null. A different default can be "
"specified:"
msgstr ""
"El valor per defecte dels diccionaris Godot és nul. Es pot especificar un "
"valor predeterminat diferent:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:601
msgid "Exporting C# arrays"
msgstr "Exportació de matrius de C#"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:603
msgid ""
"C# arrays can exported as long as the element type is a :ref:`Variant-"
"compatible type <c_sharp_variant_compatible_types>`."
msgstr ""
"Les matrius C# es poden exportar sempre que el tipus d'element sigui "
"un :ref:`Tipus compatible amb variants <c_sharp_variant_compatible_types>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:613
msgid ""
"The default value of C# arrays is null. A different default can be specified:"
msgstr ""
"El valor predeterminat de les matrius C# és nul. Es pot especificar un valor "
"predeterminat diferent:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:627
msgid ""
"When changing an exported variable's value from a script "
"in :ref:`doc_gdscript_tool_mode`, the value in the inspector won't be "
"updated automatically. To update it, call :ref:`NotifyPropertyListChanged() "
"<class_Object_method_notify_property_list_changed>` after setting the "
"exported variable's value."
msgstr ""
"Quan es canvia el valor d'una variable exportada d'un script "
"a :ref:`doc_gdscript_tool_mode`, el valor de l'inspector no s'actualitzarà "
"automàticament. Per actualitzar-lo, truqueu "
"a :ref:`NotifyPropertyListChanged() "
"<class_Object_method_notify_property_list_changed>` després d'establir el "
"valor de la variable exportada."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:640
msgid ""
"Before reading further, you should get familiar with the way properties are "
"handled and how they can be customized with :ref:`_Set() "
"<class_Object_private_method__set>`, :ref:`_Get() "
"<class_Object_private_method__get>`, and :ref:`_GetPropertyList() "
"<class_Object_private_method__get_property_list>` methods as described "
"in :ref:`doc_accessing_data_or_logic_from_object`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_exports.rst:650
msgid ""
"The script must operate in the ``tool`` mode so the above methods can work "
"from within the editor."
msgstr ""
"L'script ha de funcionar en el mode ``eina`` perquè els mètodes anteriors "
"puguin funcionar des de l'editor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:4
msgid "C# global classes"
msgstr "Classes globals de C#"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:6
msgid ""
"Global classes (also known as named scripts) are types registered in Godot's "
"editor so they can be used more conveniently. :ref:`In GDScript "
"<doc_gdscript_basics_class_name>`, this is achieved using the ``class_name`` "
"keyword at the top of a script. This page describes how to achieve the same "
"effect in C#."
msgstr ""
"Les classes globals (també conegudes com a scripts amb nom) són tipus "
"registrats a l'editor de Godot perquè es puguin utilitzar de manera més "
"còmoda. :ref:`A GDScript <doc_gdscript_basics_class_name>`, això "
"s'aconsegueix utilitzant la paraula clau ``class_name`` a la part superior "
"d'un script. Aquesta pàgina descriu com aconseguir el mateix efecte en C#."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:12
msgid "Global classes show up in the *Add Node* and *Create Resource* dialogs."
msgstr ""
"Les classes globals es mostren als diàlegs *Afegeix un node* i *Crea un "
"recurs*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:13
msgid ""
"If an :ref:`exported property <doc_c_sharp_exports>` is a global class, the "
"inspector restricts assignment, allowing only instances of that global class "
"or any derived classes."
msgstr ""
"Si una :ref:`propietat exportada <doc_c_sharp_exports>` és una classe "
"global, l'inspector restringeix l'assignació, permetent només les instàncies "
"d'aquesta classe global o qualsevol classe derivada."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:17
msgid "Global classes are registered with the ``[GlobalClass]`` attribute."
msgstr "Les classes globals es registren amb l'atribut ``[GlobalClass]``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:30
msgid ""
"The file name must match the class name in **case-sensitive** fashion. For "
"example, a global class named \"MyNode\" must have a file name of "
"``MyNode.cs``, not ``myNode.cs``."
msgstr ""
"El nom del fitxer ha de coincidir amb el nom de la classe de manera que "
"**distingui entre majúscules i minúscules**. Per exemple, una classe global "
"anomenada \"MyNode\" ha de tenir un nom de fitxer ``MyNode.cs``, no "
"``myNode.cs``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:34
msgid ""
"The ``MyNode`` type will be registered as a global class with the same name "
"as the type's name."
msgstr ""
"El tipus ``MyNode`` es registrarà com a classe global amb el mateix nom que "
"el nom del tipus."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:38
msgid ""
"The *Select a Node* window for the ``MyNode`` exported property filters the "
"list of nodes in the scene to match the assignment restriction."
msgstr ""
"La finestra *Selecciona un node* per a la propietat exportada ``MyNode`` "
"filtra la llista de nodes de l'escena perquè coincideixi amb la restricció "
"d'assignació."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:51
msgid ""
"If a custom type isn't registered as a global class, the assignment is "
"restricted to the Godot type the custom type is based on. For example, "
"inspector assignments to an export of the type ``MySimpleSprite2D`` are "
"restricted to ``Sprite2D`` and derived types."
msgstr ""
"Si un tipus personalitzat no està registrat com a classe global, "
"l'assignació es limita al tipus Godot en què es basa el tipus personalitzat. "
"Per exemple, les assignacions d'inspector a una exportació del tipus "
"``MySimpleSprite2D`` estan restringides a ``Sprite2D`` i tipus derivats."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:62
msgid ""
"When combined with the ``[GlobalClass]`` attribute, the ``[Icon]`` attribute "
"allows providing a path to an icon to show when the class is displayed in "
"the editor."
msgstr ""
"Quan es combina amb l'atribut ``[GlobalClass]``, l'atribut ``[Icon]`` permet "
"proporcionar un camí a una icona per mostrar quan es mostra la classe a "
"l'editor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:85
msgid ""
"The ``Stats`` class is a custom resource registered as a global "
"class. :ref:`Exporting properties <doc_c_sharp_exports>` of the type "
"``Stats`` will only allow instances of this resource type to be assigned, "
"and the inspector will let you create and load instances of this type easily."
msgstr ""
"La classe ``Stats`` és un recurs personalitzat registrat com a classe "
"global. :ref:`Exportar propietats <doc_c_sharp_exports>` del tipus ``Stats`` "
"només permetrà assignar instàncies d'aquest tipus de recurs, i l'inspector "
"us permetrà crear i carregar instàncies d'aquest tipus fàcilment."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_global_classes.rst:95
msgid ""
"The Godot editor will hide these custom classes with names that begin with "
"the prefix \"Editor\" in the \"Create New Node\" or \"Create New Scene\" "
"dialog windows. The classes are available for instantiation at runtime via "
"their class names, but are automatically hidden by the editor windows along "
"with the built-in editor nodes used by the Godot editor."
msgstr ""
"L'editor Godot amagarà aquestes classes personalitzades amb noms que "
"comencen amb el prefix \"Editor\" a les finestres de diàleg \"Crea nou "
"node\" o \"Crea una escena nova\". Les classes estan disponibles per a la "
"instanciació en temps d'execució mitjançant els seus noms de classe, però "
"les finestres de l'editor oculten automàticament juntament amb els nodes "
"d'editor integrats utilitzats per l'editor Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/index.rst:6
msgid "C++ (godot-cpp)"
msgstr "C++ (godot-cpp)"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/index.rst:8
msgid ""
"This section documents `godot-cpp <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-"
"cpp>`__, the official C++ GDExtension bindings maintained as part of the "
"Godot project."
msgstr ""
"Aquesta secció documenta `godot-cpp <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-"
"cpp>`__, els enllaços oficials de C++ GDExtension que es mantenen com a part "
"del projecte Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:4
msgid "About godot-cpp"
msgstr "Quant a Godot Engine"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:6
msgid ""
"`godot-cpp <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp>`__ are the official C+"
"+ GDExtension bindings, maintained as part of the Godot project."
msgstr ""
"`godot-cpp <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp>`__ són els enllaços "
"oficials de C++ GDExtension, que es mantenen com a part del projecte Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:9
msgid ""
"godot-cpp is built with the :ref:`GDExtension system <doc_gdextension>`, "
"which allows access to Godot in almost the same way as :ref:`modules "
"<doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>`: A lot of `engine code <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot>`__ can be used in your godot-cpp project almost exactly "
"as it is."
msgstr ""
"godot-cpp es construeix amb el :ref:`GDExtension system <doc_gdextension>`, "
"que permet l'accés a Godot gairebé de la mateixa manera que :ref:`modules "
"<doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>`: Molts `codi de motor <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot>`__ es poden utilitzar gairebé exactament al vostre "
"projecte."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:13
msgid ""
"In particular, godot-cpp has access to all functions that :ref:`GDScript "
"<doc_gdscript>` and :ref:`C# <doc_c_sharp>` have, and additional access to a "
"few more for fast low-level access of data, or deeper integration with Godot."
msgstr ""
"En particular, godot-cpp té accés a totes les funcions que "
"tenen :ref:`GDScript <doc_gdscript>` i :ref:`C# <doc_c_sharp>`, i accés "
"addicional a algunes més per a un accés ràpid a les dades de baix nivell o "
"una integració més profunda amb Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:17
msgid "Differences between godot-cpp and C++ modules"
msgstr "Diferències entre els mòduls godot-cpp i C++"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:19
msgid ""
"You can use both `godot-cpp <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp>`__ "
"and :ref:`C++ modules <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>` to run C or C++ code in a "
"Godot project."
msgstr ""
"Podeu utilitzar tant els mòduls `godot-cpp <https://github.com/godotengine/"
"godot-cpp>`__ com :ref:`C++ <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>` per executar codi C "
"o C++ en un projecte Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:22
msgid ""
"They also both allow you to integrate third-party libraries into Godot. The "
"one you should choose depends on your needs."
msgstr ""
"També tots dos us permeten integrar biblioteques de tercers a Godot. El que "
"heu de triar depèn de les vostres necessitats."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:26
msgid "Advantages of godot-cpp"
msgstr "Avantatges de godot-cpp"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:28
msgid ""
"Unlike modules, godot-cpp (and GDExtensions, in general) don't require "
"compiling the engine's source code, making it easier to distribute your "
"work. It gives you access to most of the API available to GDScript and C#, "
"allowing you to code game logic with full control regarding performance. "
"It's ideal if you need high-performance code you'd like to distribute as an "
"add-on in the :ref:`asset library <doc_what_is_assetlib>`."
msgstr ""
"A diferència dels mòduls, godot-cpp (i GDExtensions, en general) no "
"requereix la compilació del codi font del motor, cosa que facilita la "
"distribució del vostre treball. Us dóna accés a la majoria de l'API "
"disponible per a GDScript i C#, cosa que us permet codificar la lògica del "
"joc amb un control total sobre el rendiment. És ideal si necessiteu codi "
"d'alt rendiment que voleu distribuir com a complement a la :ref:`biblioteca "
"d'actius <doc_what_is_assetlib>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:35
msgid "Also:"
msgstr "També:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:37
msgid ""
"You can use the same compiled godot-cpp library in the editor and exported "
"project. With C++ modules, you have to recompile all the export templates "
"you plan to use if you require its functionality at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Podeu utilitzar la mateixa biblioteca godot-cpp compilada a l'editor i al "
"projecte exportat. Amb els mòduls C++, heu de recompilar totes les "
"plantilles d'exportació que voleu utilitzar si necessiteu la seva "
"funcionalitat en temps d'execució."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:40
msgid ""
"godot-cpp only requires you to compile your library, not the whole engine. "
"That's unlike C++ modules, which are statically compiled into the engine. "
"Every time you change a module, you need to recompile the engine. Even with "
"incremental builds, this process is slower than using godot-cpp."
msgstr ""
"godot-cpp només requereix que compileu la vostra biblioteca, no tot el "
"motor. Això és a diferència dels mòduls C++, que es compilen estàticament al "
"motor. Cada vegada que canvieu un mòdul, heu de recompilar el motor. Fins i "
"tot amb les compilacions incrementals, aquest procés és més lent que "
"utilitzar godot-cpp."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:46
msgid "Advantages of C++ modules"
msgstr "Avantatges dels mòduls C++"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:48
msgid ""
"We recommend :ref:`C++ modules <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>` in cases where "
"godot-cpp (or another GDExtension system) isn't enough:"
msgstr ""
"Recomanem :ref:`Mòduls C++ <doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>` en els casos en què "
"godot-cpp (o un altre sistema GDExtension) no sigui suficient:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:51
msgid ""
"C++ modules provide deeper integration into the engine. GDExtension's access "
"is not as deep as static modules."
msgstr ""
"Els mòduls C++ proporcionen una integració més profunda al motor. L'accés de "
"GDExtension no és tan profund com els mòduls estàtics."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:53
msgid ""
"You can use C++ modules to provide additional features in a project without "
"carrying native library files around. This extends to exported projects."
msgstr ""
"Podeu utilitzar mòduls C++ per proporcionar funcions addicionals en un "
"projecte sense portar fitxers de biblioteca nadius. Això s'estén als "
"projectes exportats."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:58
msgid ""
"If you notice that specific systems are not accessible via godot-cpp but are "
"via custom modules, feel free to open an issue on the `godot-cpp repository "
"<https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp>`__ to discuss implementation "
"options for exposing the missing functionality."
msgstr ""
"Si observeu que els sistemes específics no són accessibles mitjançant godot-"
"cpp, però sí mitjançant mòduls personalitzats, no dubteu a obrir un problema "
"al `repositori godot-cpp <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp>`__ per "
"discutir les opcions d'implementació per exposar la funcionalitat que falta."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:66
#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/what_is_gdextension.rst:20
msgid "Version compatibility"
msgstr "Compatibilitat de versions"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:68
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:56
msgid ""
"GDExtensions targeting an earlier version of Godot should work in later "
"minor versions, but not vice-versa. For example, a GDExtension targeting "
"Godot 4.2 should work just fine in Godot 4.3, but one targeting Godot 4.3 "
"won't work in Godot 4.2."
msgstr ""
"Les GDextensions orientades a una versió anterior de Godot haurien de "
"funcionar en versions menors posteriors, però no a l'inrevés. Per exemple, "
"una GDExtension orientada a Godot 4.2 hauria de funcionar bé a Godot 4.3, "
"però una que tingui com a objectiu Godot 4.3 no funcionarà a Godot 4.2."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:72
msgid ""
"For this reason, when creating GDExtensions, you may want to target the "
"lowest version of Godot that has the features you need, *not* the most "
"recent version of Godot. This can save you from needing to create multiple "
"builds for different versions of Godot."
msgstr ""
"Per aquest motiu, quan creeu GDExtensions, és possible que vulgueu orientar-"
"vos a la versió més baixa de Godot que tingui les funcions que necessiteu, "
"*no* la versió més recent de Godot. Això us pot evitar la necessitat de "
"crear diverses compilacions per a diferents versions de Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:76
#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:60
msgid ""
"There is one exception to this: extensions targeting Godot 4.0 will **not** "
"work with Godot 4.1 and later "
"(see :ref:`updating_your_gdextension_for_godot_4_1`)."
msgstr ""
"Hi ha una excepció a això: les extensions orientades a Godot 4.0 **no** "
"funcionaran amb Godot 4.1 i posteriors "
"(vegeu :ref:`actualitzar_la_vostra_gdextension_per_godot_4_1`)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:79
msgid ""
"GDExtensions are also only compatible with engine builds that use the same "
"level of floating-point precision the extension was compiled for. This means "
"that if you use an engine build with double-precision floats, the extension "
"must also be compiled for double-precision floats and use an "
"``extension_api.json`` file generated by your custom engine build. "
"See :ref:`doc_large_world_coordinates` for details."
msgstr ""
"Les GDExtensions també només són compatibles amb les compilacions de motors "
"que utilitzen el mateix nivell de precisió de coma flotant per al qual es va "
"compilar l'extensió. Això vol dir que si utilitzeu una compilació de motor "
"amb flotants de doble precisió, l'extensió també s'ha de compilar per a "
"flotacions de doble precisió i utilitzar un fitxer ``extension_api.json`` "
"generat per la vostra compilació de motor personalitzada. "
"Vegeu :ref:`doc_large_world_coordinates` per a més detalls."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/about_godot_cpp.rst:86
msgid ""
"Generally speaking, if you build a custom version of Godot, you should "
"generate an ``extension_api.json`` from it for your GDExtensions, because it "
"may have some differences from official Godot builds. You can learn more "
"about the process of using custom ``extension_api.json`` files in "
"the :ref:`build system section <doc_godot_cpp_build_system>`."
msgstr ""
"En termes generals, si creeu una versió personalitzada de Godot, hauríeu de "
"generar-ne un ``extension_api.json`` per a les vostres GDExtensions, perquè "
"pot tenir algunes diferències amb les compilacions oficials de Godot. Podeu "
"obtenir més informació sobre el procés d'utilitzar fitxers "
"``extension_api.json`` personalitzats a la secció :ref:`build system "
"<doc_godot_cpp_build_system>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:7
msgid "Workflow overview"
msgstr "Visió general del flux de treball"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:9
msgid ""
"As a GDExtension, godot-cpp is more complicated to use than :ref:`GDScript "
"<doc_gdscript>` and :ref:`C# <doc_c_sharp>`. If you decide to work with it, "
"here's what to expect your workflow to look like:"
msgstr ""
"Com a extensió GDE, godot-cpp és més complicat d'utilitzar "
"que :ref:`GDScript <doc_gdscript>` i :ref:`C# <doc_c_sharp>`. Si decidiu "
"treballar-hi, aquí teniu el que semblarà el vostre flux de treball:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:12
msgid ""
"Create a new godot-cpp project (from the `template <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot-cpp-template>`__, or from scratch, as explained below)."
msgstr ""
"Creeu un nou projecte godot-cpp (des de la `plantilla <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot-cpp-template>`__, o des de zero, com s'explica a "
"continuació)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:13
msgid ""
"Develop your code with your :ref:`favorite IDE <toc-devel-"
"configuring_an_ide>` locally."
msgstr ""
"Desenvolupeu el vostre codi amb el vostre :ref:`IDE favorit <toc-devel-"
"configuring_an_ide>` localment."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:14
msgid "Build and test your code with the earliest compatible Godot version."
msgstr ""
"Creeu i proveu el vostre codi amb la versió de Godot compatible més antiga."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:15
msgid ""
"Create builds for all platforms you want to support (e.g. using `GitHub "
"Actions <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp-template/blob/main/.github/"
"workflows/make_build.yml>`__)."
msgstr ""
"Creeu compilacions per a totes les plataformes que vulgueu donar suport (p. "
"ex., utilitzant `GitHub Actions <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp-"
"template/blob/main/.github/workflows/make_build.yml>`__)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:16
msgid ""
"Optional: Publish on the `Godot Asset Library <https://godotengine.org/asset-"
"library/asset>`__."
msgstr ""
"Opcional: publiqueu-ho a la `Biblioteca d'actius del Godot <https://"
"godotengine.org/asset-library/asset>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:21
msgid ""
"For your first godot-cpp project, we recommend starting with this guide to "
"understand the technology involved with godot-cpp. After you're done, you "
"can use the `godot-cpp template <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp-"
"template>`__, which has better coverage of features, such as a GitHub action "
"pipeline and useful ``SConstruct`` boilerplate code. However, the template "
"does not explain itself to a high level of detail, which is why we recommend "
"going through this guide first."
msgstr ""
"Per al vostre primer projecte godot-cpp, us recomanem que comenci amb "
"aquesta guia per entendre la tecnologia implicada amb godot-cpp. Un cop "
"hàgiu acabat, podeu utilitzar la `plantilla godot-cpp <https://github.com/"
"godotengine/godot-cpp-template>`__, que té una millor cobertura de "
"característiques, com ara una canalització d'accions de GitHub i un codi "
"útil ``SConstruct``. No obstant això, la plantilla no s'explica amb un alt "
"nivell de detall, per això us recomanem que primer reviseu aquesta guia."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:30
#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:24
msgid "There are a few prerequisites you'll need:"
msgstr "Hi ha uns quants requisits previs que necessitareu:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:32
msgid "A Godot 4 executable."
msgstr "Un executable Godot 4."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:33
msgid "A C++ compiler."
msgstr "Un compilador C++."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:34
#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:28
msgid "SCons as a build tool."
msgstr "SCons com a eina de creació."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:35
msgid ""
"A copy of the `godot-cpp repository <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-"
"cpp>`__."
msgstr ""
"Una còpia del `repositori godot-cpp <https://github.com/godotengine/godot-"
"cpp>`__."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:37
msgid ""
"See also :ref:`Configuring an IDE <toc-devel-configuring_an_ide>` "
"and :ref:`Compiling <toc-devel-compiling>` as the build tools are identical "
"to the ones you need to compile Godot from source."
msgstr ""
"Vegeu també :ref:`Configuració d'un IDE <toc-devel-configuring_an_ide>` "
"i :ref:`Compilació de <toc-devel-compiling>`, ja que les eines de compilació "
"són idèntiques a les que necessiteu per compilar Godot des del codi font."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:41
msgid ""
"You can download the `godot-cpp repository <https://github.com/godotengine/"
"godot-cpp>`__ from GitHub or let Git do the work for you. Note that this "
"repository has different branches for different versions of Godot. "
"GDExtensions will not work in older versions of Godot (only Godot 4 and up) "
"and vice versa, so make sure you download the correct branch."
msgstr ""
"Podeu descarregar el repositori `godot-cpp <https://github.com/godotengine/"
"godot-cpp>`__ de GitHub o deixar que Git faci la feina per vosaltres. "
"Tingueu en compte que aquest dipòsit té diferents branques per a diferents "
"versions de Godot. GDExtensions no funcionarà en versions anteriors de Godot "
"(només Godot 4 i posteriors) i viceversa, així que assegureu-vos de "
"descarregar la branca correcta."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:46
msgid ""
"To use `GDExtension <https://godotengine.org/article/introducing-gd-"
"extensions>`__ you need to use the godot-cpp branch that matches the version "
"of Godot that you are targeting. For example, if you're targeting Godot 4.1, "
"use the ``4.1`` branch. Throughout this tutorial we use ``4.x``, which will "
"need to be replaced with the version of Godot you are targeting."
msgstr ""
"Per utilitzar `GDExtension <https://godotengine.org/article/introducing-gd-"
"extensions>`__ cal que utilitzeu la branca godot-cpp que coincideixi amb la "
"versió de Godot a la qual esteu orientant. Per exemple, si us orienteu a "
"Godot 4.1, utilitzeu la branca ``4.1``. Al llarg d'aquest tutorial fem "
"servir ``4.x``, que s'haurà de substituir per la versió de Godot a la qual "
"us dirigiu."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:52
msgid ""
"The ``master`` branch is the development branch which is updated regularly "
"to work with Godot's ``master`` branch."
msgstr ""
"La branca ``mestra`` és la branca de desenvolupament que s'actualitza "
"regularment per treballar amb la branca ``mestra`` de Godot."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:63
msgid ""
"If you are versioning your project using Git, it is recommended to add it as "
"a Git submodule:"
msgstr ""
"Si esteu versionant el vostre projecte amb Git, es recomana afegir-lo com a "
"submòdul de Git:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:75
msgid "Alternatively, you can also clone it to the project folder:"
msgstr "Alternativament, també podeu clonar-lo a la carpeta del projecte:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:85
msgid ""
"If you decide to download the repository or clone it into your folder, make "
"sure to keep the folder layout the same as we've setup here. Much of the "
"code we'll be showcasing here assumes the project has this layout."
msgstr ""
"Si decidiu descarregar el dipòsit o clonar-lo a la vostra carpeta, assegureu-"
"vos de mantenir el disseny de la carpeta igual que el que hem configurat "
"aquí. Gran part del codi que mostrarem aquí suposa que el projecte té aquest "
"disseny."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:89
msgid ""
"If you cloned the example from the link specified in the introduction, the "
"submodules are not automatically initialized. You will need to execute the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Si heu clonat l'exemple des de l'enllaç especificat a la introducció, els "
"submòduls no s'inicialitzen automàticament. Haureu d'executar les ordres "
"següents:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:98
msgid "This will initialize the repository in your project folder."
msgstr "Això inicialitzarà el repositori a la carpeta del vostre projecte."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:101
msgid "Creating a simple plugin"
msgstr "Creació d'un connector senzill"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:103
msgid ""
"Now it's time to build an actual plugin. We'll start by creating an empty "
"Godot project in which we'll place a few files."
msgstr ""
"Ara és el moment de crear un complement real. Començarem creant un projecte "
"Godot buit en el qual col·locarem uns quants fitxers."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:106
msgid ""
"Open Godot and create a new project. For this example, we will place it in a "
"folder called ``project`` inside our GDExtension's folder structure."
msgstr ""
"Open Godot and create a new project. Per a aquest exemple, el col·locarem en "
"una carpeta anomenada ``projecte`` dins de l'estructura de carpetes de la "
"nostra GDExtension."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:109
msgid ""
"In our project, we'll create a scene containing a Node called \"Main\" and "
"we'll save it as ``main.tscn``. We'll come back to that later."
msgstr ""
"En el nostre projecte, crearem una escena que contingui un node anomenat "
"\"Main\" i la desarem com a ``main.tscn``. Hi tornarem més endavant."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:112
msgid ""
"Back in the top-level GDExtension module folder, we're also going to create "
"a subfolder called ``src`` in which we'll place our source files."
msgstr ""
"De nou a la carpeta del mòdul GDExtension de nivell superior, també crearem "
"una subcarpeta anomenada ``src`` en la qual col·locarem els nostres fitxers "
"font."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:115
msgid ""
"You should now have ``project``, ``godot-cpp``, and ``src`` directories in "
"your GDExtension module."
msgstr ""
"Ara hauríeu de tenir directoris ``projecte``, ``godot-cpp`` i ``src`` al "
"vostre mòdul GDExtension."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:118
msgid "Your folder structure should now look like this:"
msgstr "La vostra estructura de carpetes hauria de semblar ara:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:130
msgid ""
"In the ``src`` folder, we'll start with creating our header file for the "
"GDExtension node we'll be creating. We will name it ``gdexample.h``:"
msgstr ""
"A la carpeta ``src``, començarem per crear el nostre fitxer de capçalera per "
"al node GDExtension que crearem. L'anomenarem ``gdexample.h``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:133
msgid "gdextension_cpp_example/src/gdexample.h"
msgstr "gdextension_cpp_example/src/gdexample.h"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:160
msgid ""
"There are a few things of note to the above. We include ``sprite2d.hpp`` "
"which contains bindings to the Sprite2D class. We'll be extending this class "
"in our module."
msgstr ""
"Hi ha algunes coses a destacar a l'anterior. Incloem ``sprite2d.hpp`` que "
"conté enllaços a la classe Sprite2D. Ampliarem aquesta classe al nostre "
"mòdul."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:164
msgid ""
"We're using the namespace ``godot``, since everything in GDExtension is "
"defined within this namespace."
msgstr ""
"Estem utilitzant l'espai de noms ``godot``, ja que tot a GDExtension es "
"defineix dins d'aquest espai de noms."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:167
msgid ""
"Then we have our class definition, which inherits from our Sprite2D through "
"a container class. We'll see a few side effects of this later on. The "
"``GDCLASS`` macro sets up a few internal things for us."
msgstr ""
"Aleshores tenim la nostra definició de classe, que hereta del nostre "
"Sprite2D mitjançant una classe de contenidor. Veurem alguns efectes "
"secundaris d'això més endavant. La macro ``GDCLASS`` ens configura algunes "
"coses internes."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:171
msgid "After that, we declare a single member variable called ``time_passed``."
msgstr ""
"Després d'això, declarem una variable d'un sol membre anomenada "
"``time_passed``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:173
msgid ""
"In the next block we're defining our methods, we have our constructor and "
"destructor defined, but there are two other functions that will likely look "
"familiar to some, and one new method."
msgstr ""
"En el següent bloc estem definint els nostres mètodes, tenim definits el "
"nostre constructor i destructor, però hi ha altres dues funcions que "
"probablement els semblaran familiars i un mètode nou."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:177
msgid ""
"The first is ``_bind_methods``, which is a static function that Godot will "
"call to find out which methods can be called and which properties it "
"exposes. The second is our ``_process`` function, which will work exactly "
"the same as the ``_process`` function you're used to in GDScript."
msgstr ""
"El primer és ``_bind_methods``, que és una funció estàtica que Godot cridarà "
"per esbrinar quins mètodes es poden cridar i quines propietats exposa. La "
"segona és la nostra funció ``_process``, que funcionarà exactament igual que "
"la funció ``_process`` a la qual esteu acostumats a GDScript."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:182
msgid "Let's implement our functions by creating our ``gdexample.cpp`` file:"
msgstr ""
"Implementem les nostres funcions creant el nostre fitxer ``gdexample.cpp``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:184
msgid "gdextension_cpp_example/src/gdexample.cpp"
msgstr "gdextension_cpp_example/src/gdexample.cpp"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:212
msgid ""
"This one should be straightforward. We're implementing each method of our "
"class that we defined in our header file."
msgstr ""
"Aquest hauria de ser senzill. Estem implementant cada mètode de la nostra "
"classe que hem definit al nostre fitxer de capçalera."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:215
msgid ""
"Note our ``_process`` function, which keeps track of how much time has "
"passed and calculates a new position for our sprite using a sine and cosine "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Tingueu en compte la nostra funció ``_process``, que fa un seguiment de "
"quant de temps ha passat i calcula una nova posició per al nostre sprite "
"mitjançant una funció sinus i cosinus."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:218
msgid ""
"There is one more C++ file we need; we'll name it ``register_types.cpp``. "
"Our GDExtension plugin can contain multiple classes, each with their own "
"header and source file like we've implemented ``GDExample`` up above. What "
"we need now is a small bit of code that tells Godot about all the classes in "
"our GDExtension plugin."
msgstr ""
"Hi ha un fitxer C++ més que necessitem; l'anomenarem ``register_types.cpp``. "
"El nostre connector GDExtension pot contenir diverses classes, cadascuna amb "
"la seva pròpia capçalera i fitxer font, tal com hem implementat "
"``GDExample`` més amunt. El que necessitem ara és una petita part de codi "
"que expliqui a Godot totes les classes del nostre connector GDExtension."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:224
msgid "gdextension_cpp_example/src/register_types.cpp"
msgstr "gdextension_cpp_example/src/register_types.cpp"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:264
msgid ""
"The ``initialize_example_module`` and ``uninitialize_example_module`` "
"functions get called respectively when Godot loads our plugin and when it "
"unloads it. All we're doing here is parse through the functions in our "
"bindings module to initialize them, but you might have to set up more things "
"depending on your needs. We call the ``GDREGISTER_CLASS`` macro for each of "
"our classes in our library."
msgstr ""
"Les funcions ``initialize_example_module`` i ``uninitialize_example_module`` "
"es criden respectivament quan Godot carrega el nostre connector i quan el "
"descarrega. Tot el que estem fent aquí és analitzar les funcions del nostre "
"mòdul d'enllaços per inicialitzar-les, però potser haureu de configurar més "
"coses segons les vostres necessitats. Anomenem la macro ``GDREGISTER_CLASS`` "
"per a cadascuna de les nostres classes a la nostra biblioteca."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:272
msgid ""
"You can find information about ``GDREGISTER_CLASS`` (and alternatives) "
"at :ref:`doc_object_class`."
msgstr ""
"Podeu trobar informació sobre ``GDREGISTER_CLASS`` (i alternatives) "
"a :ref:`doc_object_class`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:274
msgid ""
"The important function is the third function called "
"``example_library_init``. We first call a function in our bindings library "
"that creates an initialization object. This object registers the "
"initialization and termination functions of the GDExtension. Furthermore, it "
"sets the level of initialization (core, servers, scene, editor, level)."
msgstr ""
"La funció important és la tercera funció anomenada ``example_library_init``. "
"Primer cridem una funció a la nostra biblioteca d'enllaços que crea un "
"objecte d'inicialització. Aquest objecte registra les funcions "
"d'inicialització i terminació de la GDExtension. A més, estableix el nivell "
"d'inicialització (nucli, servidors, escena, editor, nivell)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:279
msgid ""
"At last, we need the header file for the ``register_types.cpp`` named "
"``register_types.h``."
msgstr ""
"Per fi, necessitem el fitxer de capçalera per al ``register_types.cpp`` "
"anomenat ``register_types.h``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:282
msgid "gdextension_cpp_example/src/register_types.h"
msgstr "gdextension_cpp_example/src/register_types.h"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:295
msgid "Compiling the plugin"
msgstr "Compilant el connector"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:297
msgid ""
"To compile the project we need to define how SCons using should compile it "
"using an ``SConstruct`` file which references the one in ``godot-cpp``. "
"Writing it from scratch is outside the scope of this tutorial, but you "
"can :download:`the SConstruct file we prepared <files/cpp_example/"
"SConstruct>`. We'll cover a more customizable, detailed example on how to "
"use these build files in a subsequent tutorial."
msgstr ""
"Per compilar el projecte hem de definir com s'ha de compilar amb SCons "
"utilitzant un fitxer ``SConstruct`` que fa referència al de ``godot-cpp``. "
"Escriure-lo des de zero està fora de l'abast d'aquest tutorial, però "
"podeu :descarregar:`el fitxer SConstruct que hem preparat <files/cpp_example/"
"SConstruct>`. Cobrirem un exemple detallat i més personalitzable sobre com "
"utilitzar aquests fitxers de compilació en un tutorial posterior."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:306
msgid ""
"This ``SConstruct`` file was written to be used with the latest ``godot-"
"cpp`` master, you may need to make small changes using it with older "
"versions or refer to the ``SConstruct`` file in the Godot 4.x documentation."
msgstr ""
"Aquest fitxer ``SConstruct`` s'ha escrit per utilitzar-lo amb l'últim mestre "
"``godot-cpp``, potser haureu de fer petits canvis utilitzant-lo amb versions "
"anteriors o consultar el fitxer ``SConstruct`` a la documentació de Godot "
"4.x."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:310
msgid ""
"Once you've downloaded the ``SConstruct`` file, place it in your GDExtension "
"folder structure alongside ``godot-cpp``, ``src``, and ``project``, then run:"
msgstr ""
"Un cop hàgiu baixat el fitxer ``SConstruct``, col·loqueu-lo a la vostra "
"estructura de carpetes GDExtension al costat de ``godot-cpp``, ``src`` i "
"``projecte`` i, a continuació, executeu:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:317
msgid ""
"You can omit the ``platform`` option if you are compiling for the platform "
"you are currently using. The list of available ``platform`` options depends "
"on which platform dependencies are set up (use ``platform=list`` to see all "
"available platforms). See :ref:`doc_introduction_to_the_buildsystem` for "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Podeu ometre l'opció ``plataforma`` si esteu compilant per a la plataforma "
"que esteu utilitzant actualment. La llista d'opcions de ``plataforma`` "
"disponibles depèn de les dependències de la plataforma configurades "
"(utilitza ``platform=list`` per veure totes les plataformes disponibles). "
"Vegeu :ref:`doc_introduction_to_the_buildsystem` per a més detalls."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:322
msgid ""
"You should now be able to find the compiled library in ``project/bin/``."
msgstr ""
"Ara hauríeu de poder trobar la biblioteca compilada a ``project/bin/``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:326
msgid ""
"Here, we've compiled both godot-cpp and our gdexample library as debug "
"builds, which is the default. For optimized builds, you should compile them "
"using the ``target=template_release`` option."
msgstr ""
"Aquí, hem compilat tant godot-cpp com la nostra biblioteca gdexample com a "
"compilacions de depuració, que és la predeterminada. Per a les compilacions "
"optimitzades, hauríeu de compilar-les utilitzant l'opció "
"``target=template_release``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:331
msgid "Using the GDExtension module"
msgstr "Ús del mòdul GDExtension"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:333
msgid ""
"Before we jump back into Godot, we need to create one more file in ``project/"
"bin/``."
msgstr ""
"Abans de tornar a Godot, hem de crear un fitxer més a ``project/bin/``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:336
msgid ""
"This file lets Godot know what dynamic libraries should be loaded for each "
"platform and the entry function for the module. It is called "
"``gdexample.gdextension``."
msgstr ""
"Aquest fitxer permet a Godot saber quines biblioteques dinàmiques s'han de "
"carregar per a cada plataforma i la funció d'entrada del mòdul. S'anomena "
"``gdexample.gdextension``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:362
msgid ""
"This file contains a ``configuration`` section that controls the entry "
"function of the module. You should also set the minimum compatible Godot "
"version with ``compatibility_minimum``, which prevents older version of "
"Godot from trying to load your extension. The ``reloadable`` flag enables "
"automatic reloading of your extension by the editor every time you recompile "
"it, without needing to restart the editor. This only works if you compile "
"your extension in debug mode (default)."
msgstr ""
"Aquest fitxer conté una secció de ``configuració`` que controla la funció "
"d'entrada del mòdul. També hauríeu d'establir la versió mínima compatible de "
"Godot amb ``compatibility_minimum``, que impedeix que la versió anterior de "
"Godot intenti carregar la vostra extensió. El senyalador ``recarregable`` "
"permet recarregar automàticament la vostra extensió per part de l'editor "
"cada vegada que la recompileu, sense necessitat de reiniciar l'editor. Això "
"només funciona si compileu la vostra extensió en mode de depuració (per "
"defecte)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:368
msgid ""
"The ``libraries`` section is the important bit: it tells Godot the location "
"of the dynamic library in the project's filesystem for each supported "
"platform. It will also result in *just* that file being exported when you "
"export the project, which means the data pack won't contain libraries that "
"are incompatible with the target platform."
msgstr ""
"La secció ``biblioteques`` és la part important: indica a Godot la ubicació "
"de la biblioteca dinàmica al sistema de fitxers del projecte per a cada "
"plataforma suportada. També provocarà que * només * aquest fitxer s'exporti "
"quan exporteu el projecte, el que significa que el paquet de dades no "
"contindrà biblioteques que siguin incompatibles amb la plataforma de "
"destinació."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:374
msgid ""
"You can learn more about ``.gdextension`` files "
"at :ref:`doc_gdextension_file`."
msgstr ""
"Podeu obtenir més informació sobre els fitxers ``.gdextension`` "
"a :ref:`doc_gdextension_file`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:376
msgid "Here is another overview to check the correct file structure:"
msgstr ""
"Aquí teniu una altra visió general per comprovar l'estructura correcta del "
"fitxer:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:399
msgid ""
"Time to jump back into Godot. We load up the main scene we created way back "
"in the beginning and now add a newly available GDExample node to the scene:"
msgstr ""
"És hora de tornar a saltar a Godot. Carreguem l'escena principal que vam "
"crear al principi i ara afegim un nou node GDExample disponible a l'escena:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:404
msgid ""
"We're going to assign the Godot logo to this node as our texture, disable "
"the ``centered`` property:"
msgstr ""
"Assignarem el logotip de Godot a aquest node com a textura, desactivem la "
"propietat ``centrada``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:409
msgid "We're finally ready to run the project:"
msgstr "Per fi estem preparats per executar el projecte:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:419
msgid "Adding properties"
msgstr "Afegir propietats"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:421
msgid ""
"GDScript allows you to add properties to your script using the ``export`` "
"keyword. In GDExtension you have to register the properties with a getter "
"and setter function or directly implement the ``_get_property_list``, "
"``_get`` and ``_set`` methods of an object (but that goes far beyond the "
"scope of this tutorial)."
msgstr ""
"GDScript us permet afegir propietats al vostre script mitjançant la paraula "
"clau ``exportar``. A GDExtension heu de registrar les propietats amb una "
"funció d'obtenció i configuració o implementar directament els mètodes "
"``_get_property_list``, ``_get`` i ``_set`` d'un objecte (però això va molt "
"més enllà de l'abast d'aquest tutorial)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:427
msgid ""
"Lets add a property that allows us to control the amplitude of our wave."
msgstr ""
"Afegim una propietat que ens permeti controlar l'amplitud de la nostra ona."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:429
msgid ""
"In our ``gdexample.h`` file we need to add a member variable and getter and "
"setter functions:"
msgstr ""
"Al nostre fitxer ``gdexample.h`` hem d'afegir una variable membre i funcions "
"d'obtenció i configuració:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:444
msgid ""
"In our ``gdexample.cpp`` file we need to make a number of changes, we will "
"only show the methods we end up changing, don't remove the lines we're "
"omitting:"
msgstr ""
"Al nostre fitxer ``gdexample.cpp`` hem de fer una sèrie de canvis, només "
"mostrarem els mètodes que acabem canviant, no elimineu les línies que estem "
"ometent:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:481
msgid ""
"Once you compile the module with these changes in place, you will see that a "
"property has been added to our interface. You can now change this property "
"and when you run your project, you will see that our Godot icon travels "
"along a larger figure."
msgstr ""
"Un cop compileu el mòdul amb aquests canvis al seu lloc, veureu que s'ha "
"afegit una propietat a la nostra interfície. Ara podeu canviar aquesta "
"propietat i quan executeu el vostre projecte, veureu que la nostra icona de "
"Godot viatja al llarg d'una figura més gran."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:486
msgid ""
"Let's do the same but for the speed of our animation and use a setter and "
"getter function. Our ``gdexample.h`` header file again only needs a few more "
"lines of code:"
msgstr ""
"Fem el mateix, però per la velocitat de la nostra animació i utilitzem una "
"funció d'establiment i captador. El nostre fitxer de capçalera "
"``gdexample.h`` només necessita unes quantes línies més de codi:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:501
msgid ""
"This requires a few more changes to our ``gdexample.cpp`` file, again we're "
"only showing the methods that have changed so don't remove anything we're "
"omitting:"
msgstr ""
"Això requereix uns quants canvis més al nostre fitxer ``gdexample.cpp``, de "
"nou només mostrem els mètodes que han canviat, així que no elimineu res que "
"estem ometent:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:541
msgid ""
"Now when the project is compiled, we'll see another property called speed. "
"Changing its value will make the animation go faster or slower. Furthermore, "
"we added a property range which describes in which range the value can be. "
"The first two arguments are the minimum and maximum value and the third is "
"the step size."
msgstr ""
"Ara, quan es compile el projecte, veurem una altra propietat anomenada "
"velocitat. Canviar-ne el valor farà que l'animació sigui més ràpida o més "
"lenta. A més, hem afegit un rang de propietats que descriu en quin rang pot "
"estar el valor. Els dos primers arguments són el valor mínim i màxim i el "
"tercer és la mida del pas."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:548
msgid ""
"For simplicity, we've only used the hint_range of the property method. There "
"are a lot more options to choose from. These can be used to further "
"configure how properties are displayed and set on the Godot side. You can "
"find more information on property hints "
"here :ref:`@GlobalScope<enum_@GlobalScope_PropertyHint>`."
msgstr ""
"Per simplificar, només hem utilitzat el hint_range del mètode de propietat. "
"Hi ha moltes més opcions per triar. Es poden utilitzar per configurar encara "
"més com es mostren i es configuren les propietats al costat de Godot. Podeu "
"trobar més informació sobre les pistes de propietat "
"aquí :ref:`@GlobalScope<enum_@GlobalScope_PropertyHint>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:556
msgid ""
"Last but not least, signals fully work in GDExtension as well. Having your "
"extension react to a signal given out by another object requires you to call "
"``connect`` on that object. We can't think of a good example for our "
"wobbling Godot icon, we would need to showcase a far more complete example."
msgstr ""
"Finalment, però no menys important, els senyals també funcionen completament "
"a GDExtension. Perquè la vostra extensió reaccioni a un senyal emès per un "
"altre objecte requereix que crideu a ``connect'` en aquest objecte. No se'ns "
"acudeix un bon exemple per a la nostra icona de Godot que es mou, hauríem de "
"mostrar un exemple molt més complet."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:561
msgid "This is the required syntax:"
msgstr "Aquesta és la sintaxi necessària:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:567
msgid ""
"To connect our signal ``the_signal`` from some other node with our method "
"``my_method``, we need to provide the ``connect`` method with the name of "
"the signal and a ``Callable``. The ``Callable`` holds information about an "
"object on which a method can be called. In our case, it associates our "
"current object instance ``this`` with the method ``my_method`` of the "
"object. Then the ``connect`` method will add this to the observers of "
"``the_signal``. Whenever ``the_signal`` is now emitted, Godot knows which "
"method of which object it needs to call."
msgstr ""
"Per connectar el nostre senyal ``the_signal`` des d'algun altre node amb el "
"nostre mètode ``my_method``, hem de proporcionar el mètode ``connect`` amb "
"el nom del senyal i un ``Callable``. El ``Callable`` conté informació sobre "
"un objecte sobre el qual es pot cridar un mètode. En el nostre cas, associa "
"la nostra instància d'objecte actual ``this`` amb el mètode ``my_method`` de "
"l'objecte. Aleshores, el mètode ``connect`` afegirà això als observadors de "
"``the_signal``. Sempre que ara s'emet ``the_signal``, Godot sap quin mètode "
"de quin objecte necessita cridar."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:575
msgid ""
"Note that you can only call ``my_method`` if you've previously registered it "
"in your ``_bind_methods`` method. Otherwise Godot will not know about the "
"existence of ``my_method``."
msgstr ""
"Tingueu en compte que només podeu cridar a ``my_method`` si l'heu registrat "
"prèviament al vostre mètode ``_bind_methods``. En cas contrari, Godot no "
"sabrà sobre l'existència de ``my_method``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:579
msgid ""
"To learn more about ``Callable``, check out the class reference "
"here: :ref:`Callable <class_Callable>`."
msgstr ""
"Per obtenir més informació sobre ``Callable``, consulteu la referència de la "
"classe aquí: :ref:`Callable <class_Callable>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:581
msgid ""
"Having your object sending out signals is more common. For our wobbling "
"Godot icon, we'll do something silly just to show how it works. We're going "
"to emit a signal every time a second has passed and pass the new location "
"along."
msgstr ""
"És més comú que el vostre objecte enviï senyals. Per a la nostra icona Godot "
"tambaleant, farem alguna cosa ximple només per mostrar com funciona. Emetrem "
"un senyal cada cop que passi un segon i passarem la nova ubicació."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/scripting/cpp/gdextension_cpp_example.rst:585
