#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:551
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shader_functions.rst:61
msgid ""
"The `GLSL Language Specification <http://www.opengl.org/registry/doc/"
"GLSLangSpec.4.30.6.pdf>`_ says under section 5.10 Vector and Matrix "
"Operations:"
msgstr ""
"L'especificació del llenguatge GLSL <http://www.opengl.org/registry/doc/"
"GLSLangSpec.4.30.6.pdf>`_ diu a la secció 5.10 Operacions vectorials i "
"matricials:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:553
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shader_functions.rst:63
msgid ""
"With a few exceptions, operations are component-wise. Usually, when an "
"operator operates on a vector or matrix, it is operating independently on "
"each component of the vector or matrix, in a component-wise fashion. [...] "
"The exceptions are matrix multiplied by vector, vector multiplied by matrix, "
"and matrix multiplied by matrix. These do not operate component-wise, but "
"rather perform the correct linear algebraic multiply."
msgstr ""
"Amb algunes excepcions, les operacions són per components. Normalment, quan "
"un operador opera sobre un vector o una matriu, està operant independentment "
"sobre cada component del vector o de la matriu, en funció dels components. "
"[...] Les excepcions són matriu multiplicada per vector, vector multiplicada "
"per matriu i matriu multiplicada per matriu. Aquests no funcionen per "
"components, sinó que realitzen la multiplicació algebraica lineal correcta."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:560
msgid "Flow control"
msgstr "Control de flux"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:562
msgid "Godot Shading language supports the most common types of flow control:"
msgstr ""
"El llenguatge Godot Shading admet els tipus més comuns de control de flux:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:613
msgid ""
"Keep in mind that in modern GPUs, an infinite loop can exist and can freeze "
"your application (including editor). Godot can't protect you from this, so "
"be careful not to make this mistake!"
msgstr ""
"Tingueu en compte que a les GPU modernes, pot existir un bucle infinit i pot "
"congelar la vostra aplicació (inclòs l'editor). Godot no us pot protegir "
"d'això, així que aneu amb compte de no cometre aquest error!"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:617
msgid ""
"Also, when comparing floating-point values against a number, make sure to "
"compare them against a *range* instead of an exact number."
msgstr ""
"A més, quan compareu valors de coma flotant amb un nombre, assegureu-vos de "
"comparar-los amb un *interval* en lloc d'un nombre exacte."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:620
msgid ""
"A comparison like ``if (value == 0.3)`` may not evaluate to ``true``. "
"Floating-point math is often approximate and can defy expectations. It can "
"also behave differently depending on the hardware."
msgstr ""
"Una comparació com ``si (valor == 0,3)`` pot no avaluar-se com a ``true``. "
"Les matemàtiques de coma flotant sovint són aproximades i poden desafiar les "
"expectatives. També pot comportar-se de manera diferent segons el maquinari."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:624
msgid "**Don't** do this."
msgstr "**No** ho facis."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:635
msgid ""
"Instead, always perform a range comparison with an epsilon value. The larger "
"the floating-point number (and the less precise the floating-point number), "
"the larger the epsilon value should be."
msgstr ""
"En lloc d'això, feu sempre una comparació d'intervals amb un valor "
"d'èpsilon. Com més gran sigui el nombre de coma flotant (i menys precís "
"sigui el nombre de coma flotant), més gran hauria de ser el valor d'èpsilon."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:646
msgid ""
"See `floating-point-gui.de <https://floating-point-gui.de/>`__ for more "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Vegeu `floating-point-gui.de <https://floating-point-gui.de/>`__ per obtenir "
"més informació."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:650
msgid "Discarding"
msgstr "Descart"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:652
msgid ""
"Fragment, light, and custom functions (called from fragment or light) can "
"use the ``discard`` keyword. If used, the fragment is discarded and nothing "
"is written."
msgstr ""
"Les funcions de fragment, llum i personalitzades (anomenades des de fragment "
"o llum) poden utilitzar la paraula clau ``descartar``. Si s'utilitza, el "
"fragment es descarta i no s'escriu res."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:655
msgid ""
"Beware that ``discard`` has a performance cost when used, as it will prevent "
"the depth prepass from being effective on any surfaces using the shader. "
"Also, a discarded pixel still needs to be rendered in the vertex shader, "
"which means a shader that uses ``discard`` on all of its pixels is still "
"more expensive to render compared to not rendering any object in the first "
"place."
msgstr ""
"Tingueu en compte que ``descartar`` té un cost de rendiment quan s'utilitza, "
"ja que evitarà que el prepass de profunditat sigui efectiu en qualsevol "
"superfície que utilitzi el shader. A més, un píxel descartat encara s'ha de "
"representar al vertex shader, el que significa que un shader que utilitza "
"``discard'` en tots els seus píxels encara és més car de renderitzar en "
"comparació amb no representar cap objecte en primer lloc."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:664
msgid ""
"It is possible to define functions in a Godot shader. They use the following "
"syntax:"
msgstr ""
"És possible definir funcions en un shader Godot. Utilitzen la sintaxi "
"següent:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:680
msgid ""
"You can only use functions that have been defined above (higher in the "
"editor) the function from which you are calling them. Redefining a function "
"that has already been defined above (or is a built-in function name) will "
"cause an error."
msgstr ""
"Només podeu utilitzar les funcions que s'han definit més amunt (més amunt a "
"l'editor) la funció des de la qual les esteu cridant. Redefinir una funció "
"que ja s'ha definit anteriorment (o és un nom de funció integrat) provocarà "
"un error."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:684
msgid "Function arguments can have special qualifiers:"
msgstr "Els arguments de funció poden tenir qualificadors especials:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:686
msgid "**in**: Means the argument is only for reading (default)."
msgstr "**in**: vol dir que l'argument només és per llegir (per defecte)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:687
msgid "**out**: Means the argument is only for writing."
msgstr "**fora**: vol dir que l'argument només és per escriure."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:688
msgid "**inout**: Means the argument is fully passed via reference."
msgstr ""
"**inout**: significa que l'argument es passa completament mitjançant "
"referència."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:689
msgid ""
"**const**: Means the argument is a constant and cannot be changed, may be "
"combined with **in** qualifier."
msgstr ""
"**const**: significa que l'argument és una constant i no es pot canviar, es "
"pot combinar amb el qualificador **in**."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:692
msgid "Example below:"
msgstr "Exemple a continuació:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:700
msgid ""
"Function overloading is supported. You can define multiple functions with "
"the same name, but different arguments. Note that `implicit casting "
"<Casting_>`_ in overloaded function calls is not allowed, such as from "
"``int`` to ``float`` (``1`` to ``1.0``)."
msgstr ""
"S'admet la sobrecàrrega de funcions. Podeu definir diverses funcions amb el "
"mateix nom, però amb arguments diferents. Tingueu en compte que no es permet "
"l'emissió implícita de <Casting_>`_ a les trucades de funcions "
"sobrecarregades, com ara de ``int`` a ``float`` (``1`` a ``1.0``)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:720
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/converting_glsl_to_godot_shaders.rst:59
msgid "Varyings"
msgstr "Varyings"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:722
msgid ""
"To send data from the vertex to the fragment (or light) processor function, "
"*varyings* are used. They are set for every primitive vertex in the *vertex "
"processor*, and the value is interpolated for every pixel in the *fragment "
"processor*."
msgstr ""
"Per enviar dades des del vèrtex a la funció del processador de fragments (o "
"llum), s'utilitzen *variables*. S'estableixen per a cada vèrtex primitiu del "
"*processador de vèrtex*, i el valor s'interpola per a cada píxel del "
"*processador de fragments*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:744
msgid "Varying can also be an array:"
msgstr "Variar també pot ser una matriu:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:761
msgid ""
"It's also possible to send data from *fragment* to *light* processors using "
"*varying* keyword. To do so you can assign it in the *fragment* and later "
"use it in the *light* function."
msgstr ""
"També és possible enviar dades des de *fragment* als processadors *light* "
"mitjançant la paraula clau *variant*. Per fer-ho podeu assignar-lo al "
"*fragment* i, posteriorment, utilitzar-lo a la funció *light*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:777
msgid ""
"Note that varying may not be assigned in custom functions or a *light "
"processor* function like:"
msgstr ""
"Tingueu en compte que és possible que la variació no s'assigni a les "
"funcions personalitzades o a una funció de *processador lleuger* com ara:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:797
msgid ""
"This limitation was introduced to prevent incorrect usage before "
"initialization."
msgstr ""
"Aquesta limitació es va introduir per evitar un ús incorrecte abans de la "
"inicialització."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:800
msgid "Interpolation qualifiers"
msgstr "Qualificadors d'interpolació"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:802
msgid ""
"Certain values are interpolated during the shading pipeline. You can modify "
"how these interpolations are done by using *interpolation qualifiers*."
msgstr ""
"Alguns valors s'interpolen durant la canonada d'ombrejat. Podeu modificar "
"com es fan aquestes interpolacions utilitzant *qualificadors d'interpolació*."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:819
msgid "There are two possible interpolation qualifiers:"
msgstr "Hi ha dos possibles qualificadors d'interpolació:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:822
msgid "Qualifier"
msgstr "Qualificador"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:824
msgid "**flat**"
msgstr "**pla**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:824
msgid "The value is not interpolated."
msgstr "El valor no està interpolat."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:826
msgid "**smooth**"
msgstr "**suau**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:826
msgid ""
"The value is interpolated in a perspective-correct fashion. This is the "
"default."
msgstr ""
"El valor s'interpola de manera correcta en perspectiva. Aquesta és la "
"predeterminada."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:832
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/your_first_shader/your_first_3d_shader.rst:231
msgid "Uniforms"
msgstr "Uniforms"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:834
msgid ""
"Passing values to shaders is possible with *uniforms*, which are defined in "
"the global scope of the shader, outside of functions. When a shader is later "
"assigned to a material, the uniforms will appear as editable parameters in "
"the material's inspector. Uniforms can't be written from within the shader. "
"Any :ref:`data type <doc_shading_language_data_types>` except for ``void`` "
"can be a uniform."
msgstr ""
"Passar valors als shaders és possible amb *uniforms*, que es defineixen a "
"l'àmbit global del shader, fora de les funcions. Quan més tard s'assigna un "
"shader a un material, els uniformes apareixeran com a paràmetres editables a "
"l'inspector del material. Els uniformes no es poden escriure des de l'ombra. "
"Qualsevol :ref:`tipus de dades <doc_shading_language_data_types>` excepte "
"``void`` pot ser uniforme."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:848
msgid ""
"You can set uniforms in the editor in the material's inspector. Alternately, "
"you can set them :ref:`from code "
"<doc_shading_language_setting_uniforms_from_code>`."
msgstr ""
"Podeu posar uniformes a l'editor de l'inspector de material. "
"Alternativament, podeu configurar-los :ref:`des del codi "
"<doc_shading_language_setting_uniforms_from_code>`."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:852
msgid "Uniform hints"
msgstr "Suggeriments uniformes"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:854
msgid ""
"Godot provides optional uniform hints to make the compiler understand what "
"the uniform is used for, and how the editor should allow users to modify it."
msgstr ""
"Godot proporciona pistes d'uniformes opcionals per fer que el compilador "
"entengui per a què s'utilitza l'uniforme i com l'editor hauria de permetre "
"als usuaris modificar-lo."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:866
msgid "Uniforms can also be assigned default values:"
msgstr "També es poden assignar valors per defecte als uniformes:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:875
msgid ""
"Note that when adding a default value and a hint, the default value goes "
"after the hint."
msgstr ""
"Tingueu en compte que quan s'afegeix un valor per defecte i una pista, el "
"valor predeterminat va després de la pista."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:877
msgid "Full list of uniform hints below:"
msgstr "Llista completa de consells uniformes a continuació:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:880
msgid "Hint"
msgstr "Indicació"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:882
msgid "**vec3, vec4**"
msgstr "**vec3, vec4**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:882
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:888
msgid "source_color"
msgstr "color_origen"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:882
msgid "Used as color."
msgstr "S'utilitza com a color."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:884
msgid "hint_enum(\"String1\", \"String2\")"
msgstr "hint_enum(\"Cadena1\", \"Cadena2\")"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:884
msgid "Displays int input as a dropdown widget in the editor."
msgstr "Mostra l'entrada int com a widget desplegable a l'editor."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:886
msgid "**int, float**"
msgstr "**int, flotant**"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:886
msgid "hint_range(min, max[, step])"
msgstr "hint_range(min, max[, step])"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:886
msgid "Restricted to values in a range (with min/max/step)."
msgstr "Restringit als valors d'un interval (amb mín/màx/pas)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:888
msgid "Used as albedo color."
msgstr "S'utilitza com a color d'albedo."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:890
msgid "hint_normal"
msgstr "hint_normal"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:890
msgid "Used as normalmap."
msgstr "S'utilitza com a mapa normal."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:892
msgid "hint_default_white"
msgstr "hint_default_white"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:892
msgid "As value or albedo color, default to opaque white."
msgstr "Com a valor o color d'albedo, per defecte és blanc opac."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:894
msgid "hint_default_black"
msgstr "hint_default_black"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:894
msgid "As value or albedo color, default to opaque black."
msgstr "Com a valor o color d'albedo, per defecte és negre opac."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:896
msgid "hint_default_transparent"
msgstr "hint_default_transparent"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:896
msgid "As value or albedo color, default to transparent black."
msgstr "Com a valor o color d'albedo, per defecte és negre transparent."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:898
msgid "hint_anisotropy"
msgstr "hint_anisotropia"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:898
msgid "As flowmap, default to right."
msgstr "Com a mapa de flux, per defecte a la dreta."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:900
msgid "hint_roughness[_r, _g, _b, _a, _normal, _gray]"
msgstr "hint_roughness[_r, _g, _b, _a, _normal, _gray]"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:900
msgid ""
"Used for roughness limiter on import (attempts reducing specular aliasing). "
"``_normal`` is a normal map that guides the roughness limiter, with "
"roughness increasing in areas that have high-frequency detail."
msgstr ""
"S'utilitza per limitar la rugositat a la importació (intents de reduir "
"l'àlies especular). ``_normal`` és un mapa normal que guia el limitador de "
"rugositat, amb un augment de la rugositat a les zones que tenen detalls "
"d'alta freqüència."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:904
msgid "filter[_nearest, _linear][_mipmap][_anisotropic]"
msgstr "filtre[_nearest, _linear][_mipmap][_anisotropic]"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:904
msgid "Enabled specified texture filtering."
msgstr "S'ha activat el filtratge de textures especificat."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:906
msgid "repeat[_enable, _disable]"
msgstr "repetir[_enable, _disable]"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:906
msgid "Enabled texture repeating."
msgstr "S'ha activat la repetició de textures."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:908
msgid "hint_screen_texture"
msgstr "hint_screen_texture"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:908
msgid "Texture is the screen texture."
msgstr "La textura és la textura de la pantalla."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:910
msgid "hint_depth_texture"
msgstr "hint_depth_texture"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:910
msgid "Texture is the depth texture."
msgstr "La textura és la textura de profunditat."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:912
msgid "hint_normal_roughness_texture"
msgstr "hint_normal_rugositat_textura"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:912
msgid "Texture is the normal roughness texture (only supported in Forward+)."
msgstr ""
"La textura és la textura de rugositat normal (només s'admet a Forward+)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:916
msgid "Using ``hint_enum``"
msgstr "Utilitzant ``hint_enum``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:918
msgid ""
"You can access ``int`` values as a readable dropdown widget using the "
"``hint_enum`` uniform:"
msgstr ""
"Podeu accedir als valors ``int`` com a giny desplegable llegible mitjançant "
"l'uniforme ``hint_enum``:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:924
msgid ""
"You can assign explicit values to the ``hint_enum`` uniform using colon "
"syntax similar to GDScript:"
msgstr ""
"Podeu assignar valors explícits a l'uniforme ``hint_enum`` utilitzant una "
"sintaxi de dos punts similar a GDScript:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:930
msgid ""
"The value will be stored as an integer, corresponding to the index of the "
"selected option (i.e. ``0``, ``1``, or ``2``) or the value assigned by colon "
"syntax (i.e. ``30``, ``60``, or ``200``). When setting the value with "
"``set_shader_parameter()``, you must use the integer value, not the "
"``String`` name."
msgstr ""
"El valor s'emmagatzemarà com un nombre enter, corresponent a l'índex de "
"l'opció seleccionada (és a dir, ``0``, ``1`` o ``2``) o el valor assignat "
"per la sintaxi de dos punts (és a dir, ``30``, ``60`` o ``200``). Quan "
"configureu el valor amb ``set_shader_parameter()``, heu d'utilitzar el valor "
"enter, no el nom ``String``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:937
msgid "Using ``source_color``"
msgstr "Ús de ``source_color``"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:939
msgid ""
"Any texture which contains *sRGB color data* requires a ``source_color`` "
"hint in order to be correctly sampled. This is because Godot renders in "
"linear color space, but some textures contain sRGB color data. If this hint "
"is not used, the texture will appear washed out."
msgstr ""
"Qualsevol textura que contingui *dades de color sRGB* requereix una "
"indicació ``source_color`` per tal de ser mostrada correctament. Això es deu "
"al fet que Godot es renderitza en un espai de color lineal, però algunes "
"textures contenen dades de color sRGB. Si no s'utilitza aquesta pista, la "
"textura es veurà rentada."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:944
msgid ""
"Albedo and color textures should typically have a ``source_color`` hint. "
"Normal, roughness, metallic, and height textures typically do not need a "
"``source_color`` hint."
msgstr ""
"Les textures d'albedo i de color normalment haurien de tenir una pista "
"``source_color``. Normalment, les textures normals, rugoses, metàl·liques i "
"d'alçada no necessiten una indicació de ``source_color``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:948
msgid ""
"Using ``source_color`` hint is required in the Forward+ and Mobile "
"renderers, and in ``canvas_item`` shaders when :ref:`HDR "
"2D<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/viewport/hdr_2d>` is enabled. "
"The ``source_color`` hint is optional for the Compatibility renderer, and "
"for ``canvas_item`` shaders if ``HDR 2D`` is disabled. However, it is "
"recommended to always use the ``source_color`` hint, because it works even "
"if you change renderers or disable ``HDR 2D``."
msgstr ""
"L'ús de la pista ``source_color`` és necessari als renderitzadors Forward+ i "
"Mobile, i als shaders ``canvas_item`` quan :ref:`HDR "
"2D<class_ProjectSettings_property_rendering/viewport/hdr_2d>` està "
"habilitat. La pista ``source_color`` és opcional per al renderitzador de "
"compatibilitat, i per als shaders ``canvas_item`` si ``HDR 2D`` està "
"desactivat. Tanmateix, es recomana utilitzar sempre la pista "
"``source_color``, perquè funciona encara que canvieu els renderitzadors o "
"desactiveu ``HDR 2D``."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:956
msgid "Uniform groups"
msgstr "Grups uniformes"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:958
msgid ""
"To group multiple uniforms in a section in the inspector, you can use a "
"``group_uniform`` keyword like this:"
msgstr ""
"Per agrupar diversos uniformes en una secció de l'inspector, podeu utilitzar "
"una paraula clau ``group_uniform`` com aquesta:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:966
msgid "You can close the group by using:"
msgstr "Podeu tancar el grup utilitzant:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:972
msgid ""
"The syntax also supports subgroups (it's not mandatory to declare the base "
"group before this):"
msgstr ""
"La sintaxi també admet subgrups (no és obligatori declarar el grup base "
"abans d'això):"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:981
msgid "Global uniforms"
msgstr "Uniformes globals"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:983
msgid ""
"Sometimes, you want to modify a parameter in many different shaders at once. "
"With a regular uniform, this takes a lot of work as all these shaders need "
"to be tracked and the uniform needs to be set for each of them. Global "
"uniforms allow you to create and update uniforms that will be available in "
"all shaders, in every shader type (``canvas_item``, ``spatial``, "
"``particles``, ``sky`` and ``fog``)."
msgstr ""
"De vegades, voleu modificar un paràmetre en molts shaders diferents alhora. "
"Amb un uniforme normal, això requereix molta feina, ja que s'han de fer un "
"seguiment de tots aquests shaders i l'uniforme s'ha de configurar per a "
"cadascun d'ells. Els uniformes globals us permeten crear i actualitzar "
"uniformes que estaran disponibles en tots els shaders, en cada tipus de "
"shader (``canvas_item``, ``spatial``, ``partícules``, ``sky`` i ``fog``)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:990
msgid ""
"Global uniforms are especially useful for environmental effects that affect "
"many objects in a scene, like having foliage bend when the player is nearby, "
"or having objects move with the wind."
msgstr ""
"Els uniformes globals són especialment útils per als efectes ambientals que "
"afecten molts objectes d'una escena, com ara que el fullatge es doblegui "
"quan el jugador és a prop o que els objectes es moguin amb el vent."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:994
msgid ""
"*Global uniforms* are not the same as *global scope* for an individual "
"shader. While regular uniforms are defined outside of shader functions and "
"are therefore the global scope of the shader, global uniforms are global to "
"all shaders in the entire project (but within each shader, are also in the "
"global scope)."
msgstr ""
"Els *uniformes globals* no són el mateix que *abast global* per a un shader "
"individual. Tot i que els uniformes regulars es defineixen fora de les "
"funcions de l'ombrador i, per tant, són l'àmbit global de l'ombrejat, els "
"uniformes globals són globals per a tots els ombrejats de tot el projecte "
"(però dins de cada ombrejat, també es troben en l'àmbit global)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1000
msgid ""
"To create a global uniform, open the **Project Settings** then go to the "
"**Shader Globals** tab. Specify a name for the uniform (case-sensitive) and "
"a type, then click **Add** in the top-right corner of the dialog. You can "
"then edit the value assigned to the uniform by clicking the value in the "
"list of uniforms:"
msgstr ""
"Per crear un uniforme global, obriu la **Configuració del projecte** i "
"després aneu a la pestanya **Shader Globals**. Especifiqueu un nom per a "
"l'uniforme (distingui entre majúscules i minúscules) i un tipus i, a "
"continuació, feu clic a **Afegeix** a l'extrem superior dret del diàleg. A "
"continuació, podeu editar el valor assignat a l'uniforme fent clic al valor "
"de la llista d'uniformes:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1006
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1010
msgid ""
"Adding a global uniform in the Shader Globals tab of the Project Settings"
msgstr ""
"Afegeix un uniforme global a la pestanya Shader Globals de la configuració "
"del projecte"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1012
msgid "After creating a global uniform, you can use it in a shader as follows:"
msgstr ""
"Després de crear un uniforme global, podeu utilitzar-lo en un ombrejat de la "
"següent manera:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1024
msgid ""
"Note that the global uniform *must* exist in the Project Settings at the "
"time the shader is saved, or compilation will fail. While you can assign a "
"default value using ``global uniform vec4 my_color = ...`` in the shader "
"code, it will be ignored as the global uniform must always be defined in the "
"Project Settings anyway."
msgstr ""
"Tingueu en compte que l'uniforme global *ha de* existir a la configuració "
"del projecte en el moment en què es desa l'ombrejat, o la compilació "
"fallarà. Tot i que podeu assignar un valor per defecte utilitzant ``global "
"uniform vec4 my_color = ...`` al codi shader, s'ignorarà ja que l'uniforme "
"global sempre s'ha de definir a la configuració del projecte de totes "
"maneres."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1030
msgid ""
"To change the value of a global uniform at runtime, use "
"the :ref:`RenderingServer.global_shader_parameter_set "
"<class_RenderingServer_method_global_shader_parameter_set>` method in a "
"script:"
msgstr ""
"Per canviar el valor d'un uniforme global en temps d'execució, utilitzeu el "
"mètode :ref:`RenderingServer.global_shader_parameter_set "
"<class_RenderingServer_method_global_shader_parameter_set>` en un script:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1038
msgid ""
"Assigning global uniform values can be done as many times as desired without "
"impacting performance, as setting data doesn't require synchronization "
"between the CPU and GPU."
msgstr ""
"L'assignació de valors uniformes globals es pot fer tantes vegades com es "
"vulgui sense afectar el rendiment, ja que la configuració de dades no "
"requereix sincronització entre la CPU i la GPU."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1042
msgid "You can also add or remove global uniforms at runtime:"
msgstr "També podeu afegir o eliminar uniformes globals en temps d'execució:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1049
msgid ""
"Adding or removing global uniforms at runtime has a performance cost, "
"although it's not as pronounced compared to getting global uniform values "
"from a script (see the warning below)."
msgstr ""
"Afegir o eliminar uniformes globals en temps d'execució té un cost de "
"rendiment, tot i que no és tan pronunciat en comparació amb l'obtenció de "
"valors uniformes globals d'un script (vegeu l'advertència a continuació)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1055
msgid ""
"While you *can* query the value of a global uniform at runtime in a script "
"using ``RenderingServer.global_shader_parameter_get(\"uniform_name\")``, "
"this has a large performance penalty as the rendering thread needs to "
"synchronize with the calling thread."
msgstr ""
"Tot i que *podeu* consultar el valor d'un uniforme global en temps "
"d'execució en un script utilitzant "
"``RenderingServer.global_shader_parameter_get(\"uniform_name\")``, això té "
"una gran penalització de rendiment, ja que el fil de representació s'ha de "
"sincronitzar amb el fil que crida."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1060
msgid ""
"Therefore, it's not recommended to read global shader uniform values "
"continuously in a script. If you need to read values in a script after "
"setting them, consider creating an :ref:`autoload <doc_singletons_autoload>` "
"where you store the values you need to query at the same time you're setting "
"them as global uniforms."
msgstr ""
"Per tant, no es recomana llegir contínuament els valors uniformes de l'ombra "
"global en un script. Si necessiteu llegir valors en un script després de "
"configurar-los, penseu a crear un :ref:`autoload <doc_singletons_autoload>` "
"on emmagatzemeu els valors que necessiteu consultar alhora que els "
"configureu com a uniformes globals."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1069
msgid "Per-instance uniforms"
msgstr "Uniformes per instància"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1073
msgid ""
"Per-instance uniforms are available in both ``canvas_item`` (2D) and "
"``spatial`` (3D) shaders."
msgstr ""
"Els uniformes per instància estan disponibles tant en ``canvas_item`` (2D) "
"com en ombrejats ``espacials`` (3D)."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1075
msgid ""
"Sometimes, you want to modify a parameter on each node using the material. "
"As an example, in a forest full of trees, when you want each tree to have a "
"slightly different color that is editable by hand. Without per-instance "
"uniforms, this requires creating a unique material for each tree (each with "
"a slightly different hue). This makes material management more complex, and "
"also has a performance overhead due to the scene requiring more unique "
"material instances. Vertex colors could also be used here, but they'd "
"require creating unique copies of the mesh for each different color, which "
"also has a performance overhead."
msgstr ""
"De vegades, voleu modificar un paràmetre a cada node utilitzant el material. "
"Per exemple, en un bosc ple d'arbres, quan voleu que cada arbre tingui un "
"color lleugerament diferent que es pugui editar a mà. Sense uniformes per "
"instància, això requereix crear un material únic per a cada arbre (cadascun "
"amb una tonalitat lleugerament diferent). Això fa que la gestió del material "
"sigui més complexa i també té una sobrecàrrega de rendiment a causa que "
"l'escena requereix més instàncies de material úniques. Els colors del vèrtex "
"també es podrien utilitzar aquí, però caldrien crear còpies úniques de la "
"malla per a cada color diferent, que també té una sobrecàrrega de rendiment."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1084
msgid ""
"Per-instance uniforms are set on each GeometryInstance3D, rather than on "
"each Material instance. Take this into account when working with meshes that "
"have multiple materials assigned to them, or MultiMesh setups."
msgstr ""
"Els uniformes per instància s'estableixen a cada GeometryInstance3D, en "
"comptes de cada instància de Material. Tingueu-ho en compte quan treballeu "
"amb malles que tenen diversos materials assignats o configuracions MultiMesh."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1100
msgid ""
"After saving the shader, you can change the per-instance uniform's value "
"using the inspector:"
msgstr ""
"Després de desar el shader, podeu canviar el valor de l'uniforme per "
"instància mitjançant l'inspector:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1103
#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1107
msgid ""
"Setting a per-instance uniform's value in the GeometryInstance3D section of "
"the inspector"
msgstr ""
"Establir el valor d'un uniforme per instància a la secció GeometryInstance3D "
"de l'inspector"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1109
msgid ""
"Per-instance uniform values can also be set at runtime "
"using :ref:`set_instance_shader_parameter "
"<class_GeometryInstance3D_method_set_instance_shader_parameter>` method on a "
"node that inherits from :ref:`class_GeometryInstance3D`:"
msgstr ""
"Els valors uniformes per instància també es poden establir en temps "
"d'execució mitjançant el mètode :ref:`set_instance_shader_parameter "
"<class_GeometryInstance3D_method_set_instance_shader_parameter>` en un node "
"que hereta de :ref:`class_GeometryInstance3D`:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1117
msgid ""
"When using per-instance uniforms, there are some restrictions you should be "
"aware of:"
msgstr ""
"Quan utilitzeu uniformes per instància, hi ha algunes restriccions que "
"hauríeu de tenir en compte:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1119
msgid ""
"**Per-instance uniforms do not support textures or arrays**, only regular "
"scalar and vector types. As a workaround, you can pass a texture array as a "
"regular uniform, then pass the index of the texture to be drawn using a per-"
"instance uniform."
msgstr ""
"**Els uniformes per instància no admeten textures ni matrius**, només tipus "
"escalars i vectorials regulars. Com a solució alternativa, podeu passar una "
"matriu de textures com a uniforme normal i, a continuació, passar l'índex de "
"la textura que s'ha de dibuixar amb un uniforme per instància."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1125
msgid ""
"In GLSL versions before 4.0 (i.e. GLSL 3.3 and lower), you cannot directly "
"index a texture array using a per-instance uniform, as sampler arrays can "
"only be indexed by compile-time constant expressions. This affects shaders "
"compiled with the Compatibility renderer."
msgstr ""
"A les versions de GLSL anteriors a la 4.0 (és a dir, GLSL 3.3 i anteriors), "
"no podeu indexar directament una matriu de textures utilitzant un uniforme "
"per instància, ja que les matrius de mostreig només es poden indexar "
"mitjançant expressions constants en temps de compilació. Això afecta els "
"shaders compilats amb el renderitzador de compatibilitat."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1130
msgid ""
"If you are affected, use the ``switch`` statement to select the texture:"
msgstr ""
"Si esteu afectat, utilitzeu la instrucció ``switch`` per seleccionar la "
"textura:"

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1151
msgid "There is a practical maximum limit of 16 instance uniforms per shader."
msgstr "Hi ha un límit màxim pràctic de 16 uniformes d'instàncies per shader."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1152
msgid ""
"If your mesh uses multiple materials, the parameters for the first mesh "
"material found will \"win\" over the subsequent ones, unless they have the "
"same name, index *and* type. In this case, all parameters are affected "
"correctly."
msgstr ""
"Si la vostra malla utilitza diversos materials, els paràmetres del primer "
"material de malla trobat \"guanyaran\" sobre els següents, tret que tinguin "
"el mateix nom, índex * i * tipus. En aquest cas, tots els paràmetres es "
"veuen afectats correctament."

#: ../../docs/tutorials/shaders/shader_reference/shading_language.rst:1155
msgid ""
"If you run into the above situation, you can avoid clashes by manually "
"specifying the index (0-15) of the instance uniform by using the "
"``instance_index`` hint:"
msgstr ""
"Si us trobeu amb la situació anterior, podeu evitar enfrontaments "
"especificant manualment l'índex (0-15) de l'uniforme d'instància utilitzant "
"la pista ``instance_index``:"

