msgid ""
"Successful assertions output can be enabled with the ``--success`` (``-s``) "
"option, and can be combined with any combination of filtering options above, "
"for instance:"
msgstr ""
"La sortida de les assercions correctes es pot activar amb l'opció ``--"
"success`` (``-s``), i es pot combinar amb qualsevol combinació de les "
"opcions de filtratge anteriors, per exemple:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:94
msgid ""
"Specific tests can be skipped with corresponding ``-exclude`` options. As of "
"now, some tests include random stress tests which take a while to execute. "
"In order to skip those kind of tests, run the following command:"
msgstr ""
"Es poden ometre proves específiques amb les opcions ``-exclude`` "
"corresponents. Ara mateix, algunes proves inclouen proves d'estrès "
"aleatòries que triguen una estona a executar-se. Per ometre aquest tipus de "
"proves, executeu l'ordre següent:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:103
msgid "Writing tests"
msgstr "Escriptura de proves"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:105
msgid ""
"Test suites represent C++ implementation files which must include the "
"``TEST_FORCE_LINK()`` macro. Most test suites are located directly under "
"``tests/`` directory."
msgstr ""
"Els conjunts de proves representen fitxers d'implementació C++ que han "
"d'incloure la macro ``TEST_FORCE_LINK()``. La majoria de conjunts de proves "
"es troben directament dins del directori ``tests/``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:108
msgid ""
"All test files are prefixed with ``test_``, and this is a naming convention "
"which the Godot build system relies on to detect tests throughout the engine."
msgstr ""
"Tots els fitxers de prova tenen el prefix ``test_``, i aquesta és una "
"convenció de noms en què es basa el sistema de compilació de Godot per "
"detectar proves arreu del motor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:111
msgid "Here's a minimal working test suite with a single test case written:"
msgstr ""
"Aquí teniu un conjunt de proves mínim i funcional amb un sol cas de prova "
"escrit:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:129
msgid ""
"You can quickly generate new tests using the ``create_test.py`` script found "
"in the ``tests/`` directory. This script automatically creates a new test "
"file with the required boilerplate code in the appropriate location. To view "
"usage instructions, run the script with the ``-h`` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:133
msgid ""
"The ``tests/test_macros.h`` header encapsulates everything which is needed "
"for writing C++ unit tests in Godot. It includes doctest assertion and "
"logging macros such as ``CHECK`` as seen above, and of course the "
"definitions for writing test cases themselves."
msgstr ""
"La capçalera ``tests/test_macros.h`` encapsula tot el que cal per escriure "
"proves unitàries de C++ a Godot. Inclou macros d'asserció i registre de "
"doctest com ``CHECK``, com s'ha vist abans, i, per descomptat, les "
"definicions per escriure els casos de prova mateixos."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:140
msgid ""
"`tests/test_macros.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/tests/"
"test_macros.h>`_ source code for currently implemented macros and aliases "
"for them."
msgstr ""
"`tests/test_macros.h <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/tests/"
"test_macros.h>`_ codi font de les macros implementades actualment i dels "
"seus àlies."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:143
msgid ""
"Test cases are created using ``TEST_CASE`` function-like macro. Each test "
"case must have a brief description written in parentheses, optionally "
"including custom tags which allow to filter the tests at runtime, such as "
"``[String]``, ``[Stress]`` etc."
msgstr ""
"Els casos de prova es creen amb la macro semblant a funció ``TEST_CASE``. "
"Cada cas de prova ha de tenir una descripció breu escrita entre parèntesis, "
"que pot incloure etiquetes personalitzades per filtrar les proves en temps "
"d'execució, com ara ``[String]``, ``[Stress]``, etc."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:148
msgid ""
"Test cases are written in a dedicated namespace. This is not required, but "
"allows to prevent naming collisions for when other static helper functions "
"are written to accommodate the repeating testing procedures such as "
"populating common test data for each test, or writing parameterized tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:153
msgid ""
"Godot supports writing tests per C++ module. For instructions on how to "
"write module tests, refer to :ref:`doc_custom_module_unit_tests`."
msgstr ""
"Godot permet escriure proves per mòdul C++. Per obtenir instruccions sobre "
"com escriure proves de mòdul, consulteu :ref:`doc_custom_module_unit_tests`."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:157
msgid "Subcases"
msgstr "Subcasos"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:159
msgid ""
"In situations where you have a common setup for several test cases with only "
"slight variations, subcases can be very helpful. Here's an example:"
msgstr ""
"En situacions en què teniu una configuració comuna per a diversos casos de "
"prova amb només petites variacions, els subcasos poden ser molt útils. Aquí "
"en teniu un exemple:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:173
msgid ""
"Each ``SUBCASE`` causes the ``TEST_CASE`` to be executed from the beginning. "
"Subcases can be nested to an arbitrary depth, but it is advised to limit "
"nesting to no more than one level deep."
msgstr ""
"Cada ``SUBCASE`` fa que el ``TEST_CASE`` s'executi des del principi. Els "
"subcasos es poden niar fins a una profunditat arbitrària, però es recomana "
"limitar el niament a no més d'un nivell."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:177
msgid "Assertions"
msgstr "Acció"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:179
msgid ""
"A list of all commonly used assertions used throughout the Godot tests, "
"sorted by severity."
msgstr ""
"Una llista de totes les assercions d'ús habitual a les proves de Godot, "
"ordenades per gravetat."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:183
msgid "**Assertion**"
msgstr "**Asserció**"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:185
msgid "``REQUIRE``"
msgstr "``REQUIRE``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:185
msgid ""
"Test if condition holds true. Fails the entire test immediately if the "
"condition does not hold true."
msgstr ""
"Comprova si la condició és certa. Fa fallar immediatament tota la prova si "
"la condició no és certa."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:187
msgid "``REQUIRE_FALSE``"
msgstr "``REQUIRE_FALSE``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:187
msgid ""
"Test if condition does not hold true. Fails the entire test immediately if "
"the condition holds true."
msgstr ""
"Comprova si la condició no és certa. Fa fallar immediatament tota la prova "
"si la condició és certa."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:189
msgid "``CHECK``"
msgstr "``CHECK``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:189
msgid ""
"Test if condition holds true. Marks the test run as failing, but allow to "
"run other assertions."
msgstr ""
"Comprova si la condició és certa. Marca l'execució de la prova com a "
"fallida, però permet executar altres assercions."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:191
msgid "``CHECK_FALSE``"
msgstr "``CHECK_FALSE``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:191
msgid ""
"Test if condition does not hold true. Marks the test run as failing, but "
"allow to run other assertions."
msgstr ""
"Comprova si la condició no és certa. Marca l'execució de la prova com a "
"fallida, però permet executar altres assercions."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:193
msgid "``WARN``"
msgstr "``WARN``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:193
msgid ""
"Test if condition holds true. Does not fail the test under any circumstance, "
"but logs a warning if something does not hold true."
msgstr ""
"Comprova si la condició és certa. No fa fallar la prova en cap "
"circumstància, però registra un avís si alguna cosa no és certa."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:195
msgid "``WARN_FALSE``"
msgstr "``WARN_FALSE``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:195
msgid ""
"Test if condition does not hold true. Does not fail the test under any "
"circumstance, but logs a warning if something holds true."
msgstr ""
"Comprova si la condició no és certa. No fa fallar la prova en cap "
"circumstància, però registra un avís si alguna cosa és certa."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:198
msgid ""
"All of the above assertions have corresponding ``*_MESSAGE`` macros, which "
"allow to print optional message with rationale of what should happen."
msgstr ""
"Totes les assercions anteriors tenen macros ``*_MESSAGE`` corresponents, que "
"permeten imprimir un missatge opcional amb la justificació del que hauria de "
"passar."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:201
msgid ""
"Prefer to use ``CHECK`` for self-explanatory assertions and "
"``CHECK_MESSAGE`` for more complex ones if you think that it deserves a "
"better explanation."
msgstr ""
"Preferiu ``CHECK`` per a assercions autoexplicatives i ``CHECK_MESSAGE`` per "
"a les més complexes si creieu que mereixen una explicació millor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:206
msgid ""
"`doctest: Assertion macros <https://github.com/doctest/doctest/blob/master/"
"doc/markdown/assertions.md>`_."
msgstr ""
"`doctest: macros d'asserció <https://github.com/doctest/doctest/blob/master/"
"doc/markdown/assertions.md>`_."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:211
msgid ""
"The test output is handled by doctest itself, and does not rely on Godot "
"printing or logging functionality at all, so it's recommended to use "
"dedicated macros which allow to log test output in a format written by "
"doctest."
msgstr ""
"La sortida de les proves la gestiona doctest mateix, i no depèn gens de les "
"funcions d'impressió o registre de Godot. Per tant, es recomana usar macros "
"dedicades que permeten registrar la sortida de les proves en un format "
"escrit per doctest."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:216
msgid "**Macro**"
msgstr "**Macro**"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:218
msgid "``MESSAGE``"
msgstr "``MESSAGE``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:218
msgid "Prints a message."
msgstr "Imprimeix un missatge."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:220
msgid "``FAIL_CHECK``"
msgstr "``FAIL_CHECK``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:220
msgid ""
"Marks the test as failing, but continue the execution. Can be wrapped in "
"conditionals for complex checks."
msgstr ""
"Marca la prova com a fallida, però continua l'execució. Es pot embolcallar "
"en condicionals per a comprovacions complexes."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:222
msgid "``FAIL``"
msgstr "``FAIL``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:222
msgid ""
"Fails the test immediately. Can be wrapped in conditionals for complex "
"checks."
msgstr ""
"Fa fallar la prova immediatament. Es pot embolcallar en condicionals per a "
"comprovacions complexes."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:225
msgid ""
"Different reporters can be chosen at runtime. For instance, here's how the "
"output can be redirected to an XML file:"
msgstr ""
"Es poden triar diferents reporters en temps d'execució. Per exemple, així es "
"pot redirigir la sortida a un fitxer XML:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:234
msgid ""
"`doctest: Logging macros <https://github.com/doctest/doctest/blob/master/doc/"
"markdown/logging.md>`_."
msgstr ""
"`doctest: macros de registre <https://github.com/doctest/doctest/blob/master/"
"doc/markdown/logging.md>`_."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:237
msgid "Testing failure paths"
msgstr "Prova dels camins d'error"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:239
msgid ""
"Sometimes, it's not always feasible to test for an *expected* result. With "
"the Godot development philosophy of that the engine should not crash and "
"should gracefully recover whenever a non-fatal error occurs, it's important "
"to check that those failure paths are indeed safe to execute without "
"crashing the engine."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:244
msgid ""
"*Unexpected* behavior can be tested in the same way as anything else. The "
"only problem this creates is that the error printing shall unnecessarily "
"pollute the test output with errors coming from the engine itself (even if "
"the end result is successful)."
msgstr ""
"El comportament *inesperat* es pot provar de la mateixa manera que qualsevol "
"altra cosa. L'únic problema que això crea és que la impressió d'errors "
"embrutarà innecessàriament la sortida de les proves amb errors provinents "
"del motor mateix (encara que el resultat final sigui correcte)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:249
msgid ""
"To alleviate this problem, use ``ERR_PRINT_OFF`` and ``ERR_PRINT_ON`` macros "
"directly within test cases to temporarily disable the error output coming "
"from the engine, for instance:"
msgstr ""
"Per alleujar aquest problema, useu les macros ``ERR_PRINT_OFF`` i "
"``ERR_PRINT_ON`` directament dins dels casos de prova per desactivar "
"temporalment la sortida d'errors procedent del motor, per exemple:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:265
msgid "Special tags in test case names"
msgstr "Etiquetes especials als noms dels casos de prova"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:267
msgid ""
"These tags can be added to the test case name to modify or extend the test "
"environment:"
msgstr ""
"Aquestes etiquetes es poden afegir al nom del cas de prova per modificar o "
"ampliar l'entorn de prova:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:270
msgid "**Tag**"
msgstr "**Etiqueta**"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:272
msgid "``[SceneTree]``"
msgstr "``[SceneTree]``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:272
msgid ""
"Required for test cases that rely on a scene tree with MessageQueue to be "
"available. It also enables a mock rendering server "
"and :ref:`ThemeDB<class_ThemeDB>`."
msgstr ""
"Necessària per als casos de prova que depenen que hi hagi disponible un "
"arbre d'escenes amb MessageQueue. També activa un servidor de renderitzat "
"simulat i :ref:`ThemeDB<class_ThemeDB>`."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:274
msgid "``[Editor]``"
msgstr "``[Editor]``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:274
msgid ""
"Like ``[SceneTree]``, but with additional editor-related infrastructure "
"available, such as :ref:`EditorSettings<class_EditorSettings>`."
msgstr ""
"Com ``[SceneTree]``, però amb infraestructura addicional relacionada amb "
"l'editor disponible, com ara :ref:`EditorSettings<class_EditorSettings>`."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:276
msgid "``[Audio]``"
msgstr "``[Audio]``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:276
msgid ""
"Initializes the :ref:`AudioServer<class_AudioServer>` using a mock audio "
"driver."
msgstr ""
"Inicialitza l':ref:`AudioServer<class_AudioServer>` amb un controlador "
"d'àudio simulat."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:278
msgid "``[Navigation2D]``"
msgstr "``[Navigation2D]``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:278
msgid ""
"Creates the default 2D navigation server and makes it available for testing."
msgstr ""
"Crea el servidor de navegació 2D per defecte i el posa a disposició de les "
"proves."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:280
msgid "``[Navigation3D]``"
msgstr "``[Navigation3D]``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:280
msgid ""
"Creates the default 3D navigation server and makes it available for testing."
msgstr ""
"Crea el servidor de navegació 3D per defecte i el posa a disposició de les "
"proves."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:283
msgid ""
"You can use them together to combine multiple test environment extensions."
msgstr ""
"Les podeu usar juntes per combinar diverses extensions de l'entorn de prova."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:286
msgid "Testing signals"
msgstr "Senyals"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:288
msgid "The following macros can be use to test signals:"
msgstr "Les macros següents es poden usar per provar senyals:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:294
msgid "Macro"
msgstr "Macro"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:296
msgid "``SIGNAL_WATCH(object, \"signal_name\")``"
msgstr "``SIGNAL_WATCH(object, \"signal_name\")``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:297
msgid "Starts watching the specified signal on the given object."
msgstr "Comença a observar el senyal especificat a l'objecte indicat."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:298
msgid "``SIGNAL_UNWATCH(object, \"signal_name\")``"
msgstr "``SIGNAL_UNWATCH(object, \"signal_name\")``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:299
msgid "Stops watching the specified signal on the given object."
msgstr "Deixa d'observar el senyal especificat a l'objecte indicat."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:300
msgid "``SIGNAL_CHECK(\"signal_name\", Vector<Vector<Variant>>)``"
msgstr "``SIGNAL_CHECK(\"signal_name\", Vector<Vector<Variant>>)``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:301
msgid ""
"Checks the arguments of all fired signals. The outer vector contains each "
"fired signal, while the inner vector contains the list of arguments for that "
"signal. The order of signals is significant."
msgstr ""
"Comprova els arguments de tots els senyals emesos. El vector exterior conté "
"cada senyal emès, mentre que el vector interior conté la llista d'arguments "
"d'aquest senyal. L'ordre dels senyals és significatiu."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:302
msgid "``SIGNAL_CHECK_FALSE(\"signal_name\")``"
msgstr "``SIGNAL_CHECK_FALSE(\"signal_name\")``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:303
msgid "Checks if the specified signal was not fired."
msgstr "Comprova si el senyal especificat no s'ha emès."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:304
msgid "``SIGNAL_DISCARD(\"signal_name\")``"
msgstr "``SIGNAL_DISCARD(\"signal_name\")``"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:305
msgid "Discards all records of the specified signal."
msgstr "Descarta tots els registres del senyal especificat."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:307
msgid "Below is an example demonstrating the use of these macros:"
msgstr "A continuació hi ha un exemple que demostra l'ús d'aquestes macros:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:328
msgid "Test tools"
msgstr "Eines de prova"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:330
msgid ""
"Test tools are advanced methods which allow you to run arbitrary procedures "
"to facilitate the process of manual testing and debugging the engine "
"internals."
msgstr ""
"Les eines de prova són mètodes avançats que permeten executar procediments "
"arbitraris per facilitar el procés de proves manuals i depuració dels "
"elements interns del motor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:333
msgid ""
"These tools can be run by supplying the name of a tool after the ``--test`` "
"command-line option. For instance, the GDScript module implements and "
"registers several tools to help the debugging of the tokenizer, parser, and "
"compiler:"
msgstr ""
"Aquestes eines es poden executar proporcionant el nom d'una eina després de "
"l'opció de línia d'ordres ``--test``. Per exemple, el mòdul GDScript "
"implementa i registra diverses eines per ajudar a depurar el tokenizer, "
"l'analitzador i el compilador:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:343
msgid ""
"If any such tool is detected, then the rest of the unit tests are skipped."
msgstr ""
"Si es detecta alguna d'aquestes eines, s'ometen la resta de proves unitàries."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:345
msgid ""
"Test tools can be registered anywhere throughout the engine as the "
"registering mechanism closely resembles of what doctest provides while "
"registering test cases using dynamic initialization technique, but usually "
"these can be registered at corresponding ``register_types.cpp`` sources (per "
"module or core)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:350
msgid ""
"Here's an example of how GDScript registers test tools in ``modules/gdscript/"
"register_types.cpp``:"
msgstr ""
"Aquí teniu un exemple de com GDScript registra eines de prova a ``modules/"
"gdscript/register_types.cpp``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:373
msgid ""
"The custom command-line parsing can be performed by a test tool itself with "
"the help of OS :ref:`get_cmdline_args<class_OS_method_get_cmdline_args>` "
"method."
msgstr ""
"L'anàlisi personalitzada de la línia d'ordres la pot fer la mateixa eina de "
"prova amb l'ajuda del "
"mètode :ref:`get_cmdline_args<class_OS_method_get_cmdline_args>` d'OS."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:377
msgid "Integration tests for GDScript"
msgstr "Proves d'integració per a GDScript"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:379
msgid ""
"Godot uses doctest to prevent regressions in GDScript during development. "
"There are several types of test scripts which can be written:"
msgstr ""
"Godot usa doctest per evitar regressions a GDScript durant el "
"desenvolupament. Es poden escriure diversos tipus de scripts de prova:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:382
msgid "tests for expected errors;"
msgstr "proves per a errors esperats;"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:383
msgid "tests for warnings;"
msgstr "proves per a avisos;"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:384
msgid "tests for features."
msgstr "Característiques"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:386
msgid ""
"Therefore, the process of writing integration tests for GDScript is the "
"following:"
msgstr ""
"Per tant, el procés d'escriure proves d'integració per a GDScript és el "
"següent:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:388
msgid ""
"Pick a type of a test script you'd like to write, and create a new GDScript "
"file under the ``modules/gdscript/tests/scripts`` directory within "
"corresponding sub-directory."
msgstr ""
"Trieu el tipus de script de prova que voleu escriure i creeu un fitxer "
"GDScript nou dins del directori ``modules/gdscript/tests/scripts``, al "
"subdirectori corresponent."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:392
msgid ""
"Write GDScript code. The test script must have a function called ``test()`` "
"which takes no arguments. Such function will be called by the test runner. "
"The test should not have any dependency unless it's part of the test too. "
"Global classes (using ``class_name``) are registered before the runner "
"starts, so those should work if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:398
msgid "Here's an example test script:"
msgstr "Aquí teniu un script de prova d'exemple:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:406
msgid "Change directory to the Godot source repository root."
msgstr "Canvieu al directori arrel del repositori de codi font de Godot."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:412
msgid ""
"Generate ``*.out`` files to update the expected results from the output:"
msgstr ""
"Genereu fitxers ``*.out`` per actualitzar els resultats esperats a partir de "
"la sortida:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:418
msgid ""
"You may add the ``--print-filenames`` option to see filenames as their test "
"outputs are generated. If you are working on a new feature that is causing "
"hard crashes, you can use this option to quickly find which test file causes "
"the crash and debug from there."
msgstr ""
"Podeu afegir l'opció ``--print-filenames`` per veure els noms dels fitxers "
"mentre es generen les seves sortides de prova. Si treballeu en una "
"funcionalitat nova que causa fallades greus, podeu usar aquesta opció per "
"trobar ràpidament quin fitxer de prova causa la fallada i depurar a partir "
"d'aquí."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:423
msgid "Run GDScript tests with:"
msgstr "Executeu les proves de GDScript amb:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:429
msgid "This also accepts the ``--print-filenames`` option (see above)."
msgstr "Això també accepta l'opció ``--print-filenames`` (vegeu més amunt)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:431
msgid "If no errors are printed and everything goes well, you're done!"
msgstr "Si no s'imprimeix cap error i tot va bé, ja està!"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:435
msgid ""
"Make sure the output does have the expected values before submitting a pull "
"request. If ``--gdscript-generate-tests`` produces ``*.out`` files which are "
"unrelated to newly added tests, you should revert those files back and only "
"commit ``*.out`` files for new tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:442
msgid ""
"The GDScript test runner is meant for testing the GDScript implementation, "
"not for testing user scripts nor testing the engine using scripts. We "
"recommend writing new tests for already resolved `issues related to GDScript "
"at GitHub <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues?"
"q=is%3Aissue+label%3Atopic%3Agdscript+is%3Aclosed>`_, or writing tests for "
"currently working features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/architecture/unit_testing.rst:450
msgid ""
"If your test case requires that there is no ``test()`` function present "
"inside the script file, you can disable the runtime section of the test by "
"naming the script file so that it matches the pattern ``*.notest.gd``. For "
"example, \"test_empty_file.notest.gd\"."
msgstr ""
"Si el vostre cas de prova requereix que no hi hagi cap funció ``test()`` "
"dins del fitxer de script, podeu desactivar la secció d'execució de la prova "
"posant al fitxer de script un nom que coincideixi amb el patró "
"``*.notest.gd``. Per exemple, \"test_empty_file.notest.gd\"."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/index.rst:6
msgid "Engine extension APIs"
msgstr "Compressió"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/index.rst:8
msgid ""
"This section introduces various ways in which you can extend the engine with "
"C++ code. You can use these APIs by creating a :ref:`module "
"<doc_custom_modules_in_cpp>`. Note that you can change the engine in many "
"more ways than presented here — this section just presents a subselection of "
"common and useful ways to do it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/index.rst:13
msgid ""
"Alternatively, some of the functions presented here are also available "
"through the :ref:`GDExtension <doc_what_is_gdextension>` API. You can use "
"them in C++ by creating a :ref:`godot-cpp <doc_about_godot_cpp>` based "
"GDExtension, or with any of the :ref:`community-created GDExtension "
"implementations <doc_scripting_languages>`. Note though that some aspects of "
"the code or directory structures may be different in GDExtension compared to "
"the module APIs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:4
msgid "Custom modules in C++"
msgstr "Mòduls personalitzats en C++"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:7
#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/binding_to_external_libraries.rst:7
msgid "Modules"
msgstr "Mòduls"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:9
msgid ""
"Godot allows extending the engine in a modular way. New modules can be "
"created and then enabled/disabled. This allows for adding new engine "
"functionality at every level without modifying the core, which can be split "
"for use and reuse in different modules."
msgstr ""
"Godot permet estendre el motor de manera modular. Es poden crear mòduls nous "
"i després activar-los o desactivar-los. Això permet afegir funcionalitat "
"nova al motor a qualsevol nivell sense modificar el nucli, que es pot "
"separar per usar-lo i reutilitzar-lo en mòduls diferents."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:14
msgid ""
"Modules are located in the ``modules/`` subdirectory of the build system. By "
"default, dozens of modules are enabled, such as GDScript (which, yes, is not "
"part of the base engine), GridMap support, a regular expressions module, and "
"others. As many new modules as desired can be created and combined. The "
"SCons build system will take care of it transparently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:22
#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/vendor_runtime_module.rst:13
#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_godot_servers.rst:26
#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_resource_format_loaders.rst:24
#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_audiostreams.rst:29
msgid "What for?"
msgstr "Per a què?"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:24
msgid ""
"While it's recommended that most of a game be written in scripting (as it is "
"an enormous time saver), it's perfectly possible to use C++ instead. Adding "
"C++ modules can be useful in the following scenarios:"
msgstr ""
"Tot i que es recomana que la major part d'un joc s'escrigui amb scripts (ja "
"que estalvia molt de temps), és perfectament possible usar C++ en el seu "
"lloc. Afegir mòduls C++ pot ser útil en els escenaris següents:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:28
msgid "Binding an external library to Godot (like PhysX, FMOD, etc)."
msgstr "Enllaçar una biblioteca externa amb Godot (com PhysX, FMOD, etc.)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:29
msgid "Optimize critical parts of a game."
msgstr "Optimitzar parts crítiques d'un joc."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:30
msgid "Adding new functionality to the engine and/or editor."
msgstr "Afegir funcionalitat nova al motor i/o a l'editor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:31
msgid "Porting an existing game to Godot."
msgstr "Portar un joc existent a Godot."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:32
msgid "Write a whole, new game in C++ because you can't live without C++."
msgstr "Escriure tot un joc nou en C++ perquè no podeu viure sense C++."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:37
msgid ""
"While it is possible to use modules for custom game logic, :ref:`GDExtension "
"<doc_gdextension>` is generally more suited as it doesn't require "
"recompiling the engine after every code change."
msgstr ""
"Tot i que és possible usar mòduls per a lògica de joc "
"personalitzada, :ref:`GDExtension <doc_gdextension>` sol ser més adequada, "
"ja que no requereix recompilar el motor després de cada canvi de codi."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:41
msgid ""
"C++ modules are mainly needed when GDExtension doesn't suffice and deeper "
"engine integration is required."
msgstr ""
"Els mòduls C++ són necessaris sobretot quan GDExtension no és suficient i "
"cal una integració més profunda amb el motor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:47
msgid "Creating a new module"
