msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:269
msgid "Compiling a module externally"
msgstr "Compilació externa d'un mòdul"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:271
msgid ""
"Compiling a module involves moving the module's sources directly under the "
"engine's ``modules/`` directory. While this is the most straightforward way "
"to compile a module, there are a couple of reasons as to why this might not "
"be a practical thing to do:"
msgstr ""
"Compilar un mòdul implica moure'n els fitxers font directament sota el "
"directori ``modules/`` del motor. Tot i que aquesta és la manera més directa "
"de compilar un mòdul, hi ha un parell de motius pels quals pot no ser "
"pràctic fer-ho:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:276
msgid ""
"Having to manually copy modules sources every time you want to compile the "
"engine with or without the module, or taking additional steps needed to "
"manually disable a module during compilation with a build option similar to "
"``module_summator_enabled=no``. Creating symbolic links may also be a "
"solution, but you may additionally need to overcome OS restrictions like "
"needing the symbolic link privilege if doing this via script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:283
msgid ""
"Depending on whether you have to work with the engine's source code, the "
"module files added directly to ``modules/`` changes the working tree to the "
"point where using a VCS (like ``git``) proves to be cumbersome as you need "
"to make sure that only the engine-related code is committed by filtering "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:289
msgid ""
"So if you feel like the independent structure of custom modules is needed, "
"lets take our \"summator\" module and move it to the engine's parent "
"directory:"
msgstr ""
"Així doncs, si creieu que cal l'estructura independent dels mòduls "
"personalitzats, agafem el nostre mòdul \"summator\" i movem-lo al directori "
"pare del motor:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:297
msgid ""
"Compile the engine with our module by providing ``custom_modules`` build "
"option which accepts a comma-separated list of directory paths containing "
"custom C++ modules, similar to the following:"
msgstr ""
"Compileu el motor amb el nostre mòdul proporcionant l'opció de compilació "
"``custom_modules``, que accepta una llista separada per comes de camins de "
"directoris que contenen mòduls C++ personalitzats, semblant a la següent:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:305
msgid ""
"The build system shall detect all modules under the ``../modules`` directory "
"and compile them accordingly, including our \"summator\" module."
msgstr ""
"El sistema de compilació detectarà tots els mòduls dins del directori ``../"
"modules`` i els compilarà en conseqüència, inclòs el nostre mòdul "
"\"summator\"."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:310
msgid ""
"Any path passed to ``custom_modules`` will be converted to an absolute path "
"internally as a way to distinguish between custom and built-in modules. It "
"means that things like generating module documentation may rely on a "
"specific path structure on your machine."
msgstr ""
"Qualsevol camí passat a ``custom_modules`` es convertirà internament en un "
"camí absolut per distingir entre mòduls personalitzats i integrats. Això vol "
"dir que coses com generar la documentació del mòdul poden dependre d'una "
"estructura de camins concreta a la vostra màquina."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:317
msgid ""
":ref:`Introduction to the buildsystem - Custom modules build option "
"<doc_buildsystem_custom_modules>`."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Introducció al sistema de compilació - Opció de compilació de mòduls "
"personalitzats <doc_buildsystem_custom_modules>`."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:320
msgid "Customizing module types initialization"
msgstr "Personalització de la inicialització dels tipus del mòdul"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:322
msgid ""
"Modules can interact with other built-in engine classes during runtime and "
"even affect the way core types are initialized. So far, we've been using "
"``register_summator_types`` as a way to bring in module classes to be "
"available within the engine."
msgstr ""
"Els mòduls poden interactuar amb altres classes integrades del motor durant "
"l'execució i fins i tot afectar la manera com s'inicialitzen els tipus del "
"nucli. Fins ara hem usat ``register_summator_types`` com a manera de fer que "
"les classes del mòdul estiguin disponibles dins del motor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:327
msgid ""
"A crude order of the engine setup can be summarized as a list of the "
"following type registration methods:"
msgstr ""
"Un ordre aproximat de la configuració del motor es pot resumir com una "
"llista dels mètodes de registre de tipus següents:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:346
msgid ""
"Our ``Summator`` class is initialized during the ``register_module_types()`` "
"call. Imagine that we need to satisfy some common module runtime dependency "
"(like singletons), or allow us to override existing engine method callbacks "
"before they can be assigned by the engine itself. In that case, we want to "
"ensure that our module classes are registered *before* any other built-in "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:352
msgid ""
"This is where we can define an optional ``preregister_summator_types()`` "
"method which will be called before anything else during the "
"``preregister_module_types()`` engine setup stage."
msgstr ""
"Aquí és on podem definir un mètode opcional ``preregister_summator_types()`` "
"que es cridarà abans de qualsevol altra cosa durant l'etapa de configuració "
"del motor ``preregister_module_types()``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:356
msgid ""
"We now need to add this method to ``register_types`` header and source files:"
msgstr ""
"Ara hem d'afegir aquest mètode als fitxers de capçalera i de codi font de "
"``register_types``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:367
msgid ""
"Unlike other register methods, we have to explicitly define "
"``MODULE_SUMMATOR_HAS_PREREGISTER`` to let the build system know what "
"relevant method calls to include at compile time. The module's name has to "
"be converted to uppercase as well."
msgstr ""
"A diferència d'altres mètodes de registre, hem de definir explícitament "
"``MODULE_SUMMATOR_HAS_PREREGISTER`` perquè el sistema de compilació sàpiga "
"quines crides de mètode rellevants ha d'incloure en temps de compilació. El "
"nom del mòdul també s'ha de convertir a majúscules."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:394
msgid "Writing custom documentation"
msgstr "Escriptura de documentació personalitzada"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:396
msgid ""
"Writing documentation may seem like a boring task, but it is highly "
"recommended to document your newly created module to make it easier for "
"users to benefit from it. Not to mention that the code you've written one "
"year ago may become indistinguishable from the code that was written by "
"someone else, so be kind to your future self!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:402
msgid "There are several steps in order to setup custom docs for the module:"
msgstr ""
"Hi ha diversos passos per configurar documentació personalitzada per al "
"mòdul:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:404
msgid ""
"Make a new directory in the root of the module. The directory name can be "
"anything, but we'll be using the ``doc_classes`` name throughout this "
"section."
msgstr ""
"Creeu un directori nou a l'arrel del mòdul. El nom del directori pot ser "
"qualsevol, però en aquesta secció usarem el nom ``doc_classes``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:407
msgid "Now, we need to edit ``config.py``, add the following snippet:"
msgstr "Ara hem d'editar ``config.py`` i afegir-hi el fragment següent:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:419
msgid ""
"The ``get_doc_path()`` function is used by the build system to determine the "
"location of the docs. In this case, they will be located in the ``modules/"
"summator/doc_classes`` directory. If you don't define this, the doc path for "
"your module will fall back to the main ``doc/classes`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:425
msgid ""
"The ``get_doc_classes()`` method is necessary for the build system to know "
"which registered classes belong to the module. You need to list all of your "
"classes here. The classes that you don't list will end up in the main ``doc/"
"classes`` directory."
msgstr ""
"El mètode ``get_doc_classes()`` és necessari perquè el sistema de compilació "
"sàpiga quines classes registrades pertanyen al mòdul. Heu de llistar aquí "
"totes les vostres classes. Les classes que no llistis acabaran al directori "
"principal ``doc/classes``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:432
msgid ""
"You can use Git to check if you have missed some of your classes by checking "
"the untracked files with ``git status``. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Podeu usar Git per comprovar si us heu deixat alguna classe mirant els "
"fitxers no seguits amb ``git status``. Per exemple:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:439
msgid "Example output:"
msgstr "Sortida d'exemple:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:453
msgid "Now we can generate the documentation:"
msgstr "Quant a la documentació"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:455
msgid ""
"We can do this via running Godot's doctool i.e. ``godot --doctool <path>``, "
"which will dump the engine API reference to the given ``<path>`` in XML "
"format."
msgstr ""
"Podem fer-ho executant el doctool de Godot, és a dir, ``godot --doctool "
"<path>``, que bolcarà la referència de l'API del motor al ``<path>`` indicat "
"en format XML."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:458
msgid ""
"In our case we'll point it to the root of the cloned repository. You can "
"point it to an another folder, and just copy over the files that you need."
msgstr ""
"En el nostre cas l'apuntarem a l'arrel del repositori clonat. Podeu apuntar-"
"lo a una altra carpeta i copiar només els fitxers que necessiteu."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:461
msgid "Run command:"
msgstr "Executeu l'ordre:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:467
msgid ""
"Now if you go to the ``godot/modules/summator/doc_classes`` folder, you will "
"see that it contains a ``Summator.xml`` file, or any other classes, that you "
"referenced in your ``get_doc_classes`` function."
msgstr ""
"Ara, si aneu a la carpeta ``godot/modules/summator/doc_classes``, veureu que "
"conté un fitxer ``Summator.xml``, o qualsevol altra classe que hàgiu "
"referenciat a la funció ``get_doc_classes``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:471
msgid ""
"Edit the file(s) following the `class reference primer <https://"
"docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine_details/class_reference/index.html>`__ "
"and recompile the engine."
msgstr ""
"Editeu els fitxers seguint la `guia bàsica de referència de classes <https://"
"docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine_details/class_reference/index.html>`__ "
"i recompileu el motor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:473
msgid ""
"Once the compilation process is finished, the docs will become accessible "
"within the engine's built-in documentation system."
msgstr ""
"Un cop acabat el procés de compilació, la documentació serà accessible dins "
"del sistema de documentació integrat del motor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:476
msgid ""
"In order to keep documentation up-to-date, all you'll have to do is simply "
"modify one of the XML files and recompile the engine from now on."
msgstr ""
"Per mantenir la documentació actualitzada, a partir d'ara només haureu de "
"modificar un dels fitxers XML i recompilar el motor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:479
msgid ""
"If you change your module's API, you can also re-extract the docs, they will "
"contain the things that you previously added. Of course if you point it to "
"your godot folder, make sure you don't lose work by extracting older docs "
"from an older engine build on top of the newer ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:484
msgid ""
"Note that if you don't have write access rights to your supplied ``<path>``, "
"you might encounter an error similar to the following:"
msgstr ""
"Tingueu en compte que, si no teniu permisos d'escriptura al ``<path>`` "
"proporcionat, podeu trobar un error semblant al següent:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:495
msgid "Writing custom unit tests"
msgstr "Escriptura de proves unitàries personalitzades"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:497
msgid ""
"It's possible to write self-contained unit tests as part of a C++ module. If "
"you are not familiar with the unit testing process in Godot yet, please "
"refer to :ref:`doc_unit_testing`."
msgstr ""
"És possible escriure proves unitàries autocontingudes com a part d'un mòdul "
"C++. Si encara no coneixeu el procés de proves unitàries a Godot, "
"consulteu :ref:`doc_unit_testing`."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:501
msgid "The procedure is the following:"
msgstr "La documentació principal està organitzada en les seccions següents:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:503
msgid "Create a new directory named ``tests/`` under your module's root:"
msgstr "Creeu un directori nou anomenat ``tests/`` a l'arrel del mòdul:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:511
msgid ""
"Create a new test suite: ``test_summator.h``. The header must be prefixed "
"with ``test_`` so that the build system can collect it and include it as "
"part of the ``tests/test_main.cpp`` where the tests are run."
msgstr ""
"Creeu un conjunt de proves nou: ``test_summator.h``. La capçalera ha de "
"tenir el prefix ``test_`` perquè el sistema de compilació la pugui recollir "
"i incloure-la com a part de ``tests/test_main.cpp``, on s'executen les "
"proves."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:515
msgid "Write some test cases. Here's an example:"
msgstr "Escriviu alguns casos de prova. Aquí en teniu un exemple:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:517
msgid "godot/modules/summator/tests/test_summator.h"
msgstr "godot/modules/summator/tests/test_summator.h"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/custom_modules_in_cpp.rst:547
msgid ""
"Compile the engine with ``scons tests=yes``, and run the tests with the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""
