#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:571
msgid ""
"Now we can go back to ``gdexample.c`` and define the new functions, without "
"forgetting to include the ``api.h`` header:"
msgstr ""
"Ara podem tornar a ``gdexample.c`` i definir les funcions noves, sense "
"oblidar incloure la capçalera ``api.h``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:621
msgid ""
"When instantiating an object, first we create a new Sprite2D object, since "
"that's the parent of our class. Then we allocate memory for our custom "
"struct and call its constructor. We save the pointer to the Godot object in "
"the struct as well like we mentioned earlier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:626
msgid ""
"Then we set our custom struct as the instance data. This will make Godot "
"know that the object is an instance of our custom class and properly call "
"our custom methods for instance, as well as passing this data back."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:630
msgid "Note that we return the Godot object we created, not our custom struct."
msgstr ""
"Tingues en compte que retornem l'objecte Godot que hem creat, no la nostra "
"estructura personalitzada."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:632
msgid ""
"For the ``gdextension_free_instance()`` function, we only call the "
"destructor and free the memory we allocated for the custom data. It is not "
"necessary to destruct the Godot object since that will be taken care of by "
"the engine itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:637
msgid "A demo project"
msgstr "Un projecte de demostració"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:639
msgid ""
"Now that we can create and free our custom object, we should be able to try "
"it out in an actual project. For this, you need to open Godot and create a "
"new project in the ``project`` folder. The project manager may warn you the "
"folder isn't empty if you have compiled the extension before, you can safely "
"ignore this warning this time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:645
msgid ""
"If you didn't compile the extension yet, it is the time to do it now. To do "
"that, open a terminal or command prompt, navigate to the root folder of the "
"extension and run ``scons``. It should compile quickly since the extension "
"is very simple."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:650
msgid ""
"Then, create a file called ``gdexample.gdextension`` inside the ``project`` "
"folder. This is a Godot resource that describes the extension, allowing the "
"engine to properly load it. Put the following content in this file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:666
msgid ""
"As you can see, ``gdexample_library_init()`` is the same name of the "
"function we defined in our ``init.c`` file. It is important that the names "
"match because it is how Godot calls the entry point of the extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:670
msgid ""
"We also set the compatibility minimum to 4.2, since we are targeting this "
"version. It should still work on later versions. If you are using a later "
"Godot version and rely on the new features, you need to increase this value "
"to a version number that has everything you use. "
"See :ref:`doc_what_is_gdextension_version_compatibility` for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:676
msgid ""
"In the ``[libraries]`` section we set up the paths to the shared library on "
"different platforms. Here there's only the debug versions since that's what "
"we are working on for the example. Using :ref:`feature tags "
"<doc_feature_tags>` you can fine tune this to also provide release versions, "
"add more target operating systems, as well as providing 32-bit and 64-bit "
"binaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:682
msgid ""
"You can also add library dependencies and custom icons for your classes in "
"this file, but this is out of the scope for this tutorial."
msgstr ""
"També podeu afegir dependències de biblioteca i icones personalitzades per a "
"les vostres classes en aquest fitxer, però això queda fora de l'abast "
"d'aquest tutorial."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:685
msgid ""
"After saving the file, go back to the editor. Godot should automatically "
"load the extension. Nothing will be seen because our extension only "
"registers a new class. To use this class add a ``Node2D`` as a root of the "
"scene. Move it to the middle of viewport for better visibility. Then add a "
"new child node to the root and in the **Create New Node** dialog search for "
"\"GDExample\", the name of our class, as it should be listed there. If it "
"isn't, it means that Godot didn't load the extension properly, so try "
"restarting the editor and retrace the steps to see if anything went missing."
msgstr ""
"Després de desar el fitxer, torneu a l'editor. Godot hauria de carregar "
"l'extensió automàticament. No es veurà res perquè la nostra extensió només "
"registra una classe nova. Per usar aquesta classe, afegiu un ``Node2D`` com "
"a arrel de l'escena. Moveu-lo al centre del viewport per veure'l millor. "
"Després afegiu un node fill nou a l'arrel i, al diàleg **Create New Node**, "
"cerqueu \"GDExample\", el nom de la nostra classe, que hi hauria "
"d'aparèixer. Si no hi és, vol dir que Godot no ha carregat l'extensió "
"correctament; proveu de reiniciar l'editor i repasseu els passos per veure "
"si falta alguna cosa."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:694
msgid ""
"Our custom class is derived from ``Sprite2D``, so it has a **Texture** "
"property in the Inspector. Set this to the ``icon.svg`` file that Godot "
"handily created for us when making the project. Save this scene as "
"``main.tscn`` and run it. You may want to set it as the main scene for "
"convenience."
msgstr ""
"La nostra classe personalitzada deriva de ``Sprite2D``, així que té una "
"propietat **Texture** a l'Inspector. Establiu-la al fitxer ``icon.svg`` que "
"Godot ha creat oportunament en fer el projecte. Deseu aquesta escena com a "
"``main.tscn`` i executeu-la. Potser voldreu establir-la com a escena "
"principal per comoditat."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:701
msgid ""
"Voilà! We have a custom node running in Godot. However, it does not do "
"anything and has nothing different than a regular ``Sprite2D`` node. We will "
"fix that next by adding custom methods and properties."
msgstr ""
"Voilà! Tenim un node personalitzat funcionant a Godot. Tanmateix, no fa res "
"i no té res de diferent d'un node ``Sprite2D`` normal. Ho corregirem tot "
"seguit afegint mètodes i propietats personalitzats."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:706
msgid "Custom methods"
msgstr "Mètodes personalitzats"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:708
msgid ""
"A common thing in extensions is creating methods for the custom classes and "
"exposing those to the Godot API. We are going to create a couple of getters "
"and setters which are need for binding the properties afterwards."
msgstr ""
"Una cosa habitual a les extensions és crear mètodes per a les classes "
"personalitzades i exposar-los a l'API de Godot. Crearem un parell de getters "
"i setters que seran necessaris per vincular les propietats més endavant."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:712
msgid ""
"First, let's add the new fields in our struct to hold the values for "
"``amplitude`` and ``speed``, which we will use later on when creating the "
"behavior for the node. Add them to the ``gdexample.h`` file, changing the "
"``GDExample`` struct:"
msgstr ""
"Primer, afegim camps nous a l'struct per contenir els valors de "
"``amplitude`` i ``speed``, que usarem més endavant quan creem el "
"comportament del node. Afegiu-los al fitxer ``gdexample.h``, canviant "
"l'struct ``GDExample``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:733
msgid ""
"In the same file, add the declaration for the getters and setters, right "
"after the destructor."
msgstr ""
"Al mateix fitxer, afegiu la declaració dels getters i setters just després "
"del destructor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:751
msgid ""
"In the ``gdexample.c`` file, we will initialize these values in the "
"constructor and add the implementations for those new functions, which are "
"quite trivial:"
msgstr ""
"Al fitxer ``gdexample.c``, inicialitzarem aquests valors al constructor i "
"afegirem les implementacions d'aquestes funcions noves, que són força "
"trivials:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:782
msgid ""
"To make those simple functions work when called by Godot, we will need some "
"wrappers to help us properly convert the data to and from the engine."
msgstr ""
"Per fer que aquestes funcions senzilles funcionin quan les crida Godot, "
"necessitarem alguns wrappers que ens ajudin a convertir correctament les "
"dades cap al motor i des del motor."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:785
msgid ""
"First, we will create wrappers for ``ptrcall``. This is what Godot uses when "
"the types of the values are known to be exact, which avoids using Variant. "
"We're gonna need two of those: one for the functions that take no arguments "
"and return a ``double`` (for the getters) and another for the functions that "
"take a single ``double`` argument and return nothing (for the setters)."
msgstr ""
"Primer crearem wrappers per a ``ptrcall``. Això és el que usa Godot quan se "
"sap que els tipus dels valors són exactes, cosa que evita usar Variant. En "
"necessitarem dos: un per a les funcions que no prenen arguments i retornen "
"un ``double`` (per als getters), i un altre per a les funcions que prenen un "
"únic argument ``double`` i no retornen res (per als setters)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:791
msgid "Add the declarations to the ``api.h`` file:"
msgstr "Afegiu les declaracions al fitxer ``api.h``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:799
msgid ""
"Those two functions follow the ``GDExtensionClassMethodPtrCall`` type, as "
"defined in the ``gdextension_interface.h``. We use ``float`` as a name here "
"because in Godot the ``float`` type has double precision, so we keep this "
"convention."
msgstr ""
"Aquestes dues funcions segueixen el tipus ``GDExtensionClassMethodPtrCall``, "
"tal com es defineix a ``gdextension_interface.h``. Aquí usem ``float`` com a "
"nom perquè a Godot el tipus ``float`` té doble precisió, així que mantenim "
"aquesta convenció."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:804
msgid "Then we implement those functions in the ``api.c`` file:"
msgstr "Després implementem aquestes funcions al fitxer ``api.c``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:822
msgid ""
"The ``method_userdata`` argument is a custom value that we give to Godot, in "
"this case we will set as the function pointer for the one we want to call. "
"So first we convert it to the function type, then we just call it by passing "
"the arguments when needed, or setting the return value."
msgstr ""
"L'argument ``method_userdata`` és un valor personalitzat que donem a Godot; "
"en aquest cas l'establirem com el punter de funció de la funció que volem "
"cridar. Així doncs, primer el convertim al tipus de funció i després "
"simplement el cridem passant els arguments quan calgui, o establint el valor "
"de retorn."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:827
msgid ""
"The ``p_instance`` argument contains the custom instance of our class, which "
"we gave with ``object_set_instance()`` when creating the object."
msgstr ""
"L'argument ``p_instance`` conté la instància personalitzada de la nostra "
"classe, que vam donar amb ``object_set_instance()`` en crear l'objecte."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:830
msgid ""
"``p_args`` is an array of arguments. Note this contains **pointers** to the "
"values. That's why we dereference it when passing to our functions. The "
"number of arguments will be declared when binding the function (which we "
"will do soon) and it will always include default ones if those exist."
msgstr ""
"``p_args`` és un array d'arguments. Tingueu en compte que conté **punters** "
"als valors. Per això els desreferenciem quan els passem a les nostres "
"funcions. El nombre d'arguments es declararà en vincular la funció (cosa que "
"farem aviat), i sempre inclourà els valors per defecte si n'hi ha."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:835
msgid ""
"Finally, the ``r_ret`` is a pointer to the variable where the return value "
"needs to be set. Like the arguments, it will be the correct type as "
"declared. For the function that does not return, we have to avoid setting it."
msgstr ""
"Finalment, ``r_ret`` és un punter a la variable on s'ha d'establir el valor "
"de retorn. Com els arguments, tindrà el tipus correcte segons s'hagi "
"declarat. Per a la funció que no retorna res, hem d'evitar establir-lo."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:839
msgid ""
"Note how the type and argument counts are exact, so if we needed different "
"types, for example, we would have to create more wrappers. This could be "
"automated using some code generation, but this is out of the scope for this "
"tutorial."
msgstr ""
"Observeu que els tipus i els comptadors d'arguments són exactes, així que si "
"necessitéssim tipus diferents, per exemple, hauríem de crear més wrappers. "
"Això es podria automatitzar amb generació de codi, però queda fora de "
"l'abast d'aquest tutorial."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:844
msgid ""
"While the ``ptrcall`` functions are used when types are exact, sometimes "
"Godot cannot know if that's the case (when the call comes from a dynamically "
"typed language, such as GDScript). In those situations it uses regular "
"``call`` functions, so we need to provide those as well when binding."
msgstr ""
"Tot i que les funcions ``ptrcall`` s'usen quan els tipus són exactes, de "
"vegades Godot no pot saber si és així (quan la crida prové d'un llenguatge "
"de tipatge dinàmic, com GDScript). En aquestes situacions usa funcions "
"``call`` normals, així que també les hem de proporcionar en vincular."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:849
msgid "Let's create two new wrappers in the ``api.h`` file:"
msgstr "Creem dos wrappers nous al fitxer ``api.h``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:856
msgid ""
"These follow the ``GDExtensionClassMethodCall`` type, which is a bit "
"different. First, you receive pointers to Variants instead of exact types. "
"There's also the amount of arguments and an error struct that you can set if "
"something goes wrong."
msgstr ""
"Aquests segueixen el tipus ``GDExtensionClassMethodCall``, que és una mica "
"diferent. Primer, rebeu punters a Variants en comptes de tipus exactes. "
"També hi ha la quantitat d'arguments i un struct d'error que podeu establir "
"si alguna cosa va malament."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:861
msgid ""
"In order to check the type and also extract interact with Variant, we will "
"need a few more functions from the GDExtension API. So let's expand our "
"wrapper structs:"
msgstr ""
"Per comprovar el tipus i també interactuar amb Variant, necessitarem unes "
"quantes funcions més de l'API de GDExtension. Així doncs, ampliem els "
"nostres structs de wrappers:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:881
msgid ""
"The names say all about what those do. We have a couple of constructors to "
"create and extract a floating point value to and from a Variant. We also "
"have a couple of helpers to actually get those constructors, as well as a "
"function to find out the type of a Variant."
msgstr ""
"Els noms ja ho diuen tot sobre què fan. Tenim un parell de constructors per "
"crear i extreure un valor de coma flotant cap a un Variant i des d'un "
"Variant. També tenim un parell d'auxiliars per obtenir realment aquests "
"constructors, així com una funció per esbrinar el tipus d'un Variant."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:886
msgid ""
"Let's get those from the API, like we did before, by changing the "
"``load_api()`` function in the ``api.c`` file:"
msgstr ""
"Obtenim-los de l'API, com hem fet abans, canviant la funció ``load_api()`` "
"al fitxer ``api.c``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:909
msgid ""
"Now that we have these set, we can implement our call wrappers in the same "
"file:"
msgstr ""
"Ara que ho tenim configurat, podem implementar els wrappers de crida al "
"mateix fitxer:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:965
msgid ""
"These functions are a bit longer but easy to follow. First they check if the "
"argument count is as expected and if not they set the error struct and "
"return. For the one that has one parameter, it also checks if the argument "
"type is correct. This is important because mismatched types when extracting "
"from Variant can cause crashes."
msgstr ""
"Aquestes funcions són una mica més llargues però fàcils de seguir. Primer "
"comproven si el nombre d'arguments és l'esperat i, si no ho és, estableixen "
"l'struct d'error i retornen. Per a la que té un paràmetre, també comprova si "
"el tipus de l'argument és correcte. Això és important perquè tipus no "
"coincidents en extreure de Variant poden causar fallades."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:971
msgid ""
"Then it proceeds to extract the argument using the constructor we setup "
"before. The one with no arguments instead sets the return value after "
"calling the function. Note how they use a pointer to a ``double`` variable, "
"since this is what those constructors expect."
msgstr ""
"Després extreu l'argument usant el constructor que hem configurat abans. La "
"que no té arguments, en canvi, estableix el valor de retorn després de "
"cridar la funció. Observeu que usen un punter a una variable ``double``, ja "
"que això és el que esperen aquests constructors."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:976
msgid ""
"Before we can actually bind our methods, we need a way to create "
"``GDExtensionPropertyInfo`` instances. While we could do them inside the "
"binding functions that we'll implement afterwards, it's easier to have a "
"helper for it since we'll need it multiple times, including for when we bind "
"properties."
msgstr ""
"Abans de poder vincular realment els nostres mètodes, necessitem una manera "
"de crear instàncies de ``GDExtensionPropertyInfo``. Tot i que podríem crear-"
"les dins de les funcions de vinculació que implementarem després, és més "
"fàcil tenir-ne un auxiliar, ja que el necessitarem diverses vegades, també "
"quan vinculem propietats."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:981
msgid "Let's create these two functions in the ``api.h`` file:"
msgstr "Creem aquestes dues funcions al fitxer ``api.h``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1000
msgid ""
"The first one is a simplified version of the second since we usually don't "
"need all the arguments for the property and are okay with the defaults. Then "
"we also have a function to destruct the PropertyInfo since we need to create "
"Strings and StringNames that need to be properly disposed of."
msgstr ""
"La primera és una versió simplificada de la segona, ja que normalment no "
"necessitem tots els arguments de la propietat i ens van bé els valors per "
"defecte. Després també tenim una funció per destruir el PropertyInfo, ja que "
"hem de crear Strings i StringNames que cal alliberar correctament."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1005
msgid ""
"Speaking of which, we also need a way to create and destruct Strings, so "
"we'll make an addition to existing structs in this same file. We'll also get "
"a new API function for actually binding our custom method."
msgstr ""
"Parlant d'això, també necessitem una manera de crear i destruir Strings, "
"així que farem una addició als structs existents en aquest mateix fitxer. "
"També obtindrem una funció nova de l'API per vincular realment el nostre "
"mètode personalitzat."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1029
msgid ""
"Before implementing those, let's do a quick stop in the ``defs.h`` file and "
"include the size of the ``String`` type and a couple of enums:"
msgstr ""
"Abans d'implementar-ho, fem una parada ràpida al fitxer ``defs.h`` i "
"incloguem-hi la mida del tipus ``String`` i un parell d'enums:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1065
msgid ""
"While it's the same size as ``StringName``, it is more clear to use a "
"different name for it."
msgstr ""
"Tot i que té la mateixa mida que ``StringName``, és més clar usar-hi un nom "
"diferent."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1068
msgid ""
"The enums here are just helpers to give names to the numbers they represent. "
"The information about them is present in the ``extension_api.json`` file. "
"Here we just set up the ones we need for the tutorial, to keep it more "
"concise."
msgstr ""
"Els enums d'aquí són només auxiliars per donar nom als números que "
"representen. La informació sobre aquests enums és present al fitxer "
"``extension_api.json``. Aquí només configurem els que necessitem per al "
"tutorial, per mantenir-lo més concís."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1072
msgid ""
"Going now to the ``api.c``, we need to load the pointers to the new "
"functions we added to the API."
msgstr ""
"Ara, anant a ``api.c``, hem de carregar els punters a les funcions noves que "
"hem afegit a l'API."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1093
msgid ""
"Then we can also implement the functions to create the ``PropertyInfo`` "
"struct."
msgstr ""
"Després també podem implementar les funcions per crear l'struct "
"``PropertyInfo``."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1144
msgid ""
"The simple version of ``make_property()`` just calls the more complete one "
"with a some default arguments. What those values mean exactly is out of the "
"scope of this tutorial, check the page about the :ref:`Object class "
"<doc_object_class>` for more details about binding methods and properties."
msgstr ""
"La versió simple de ``make_property()`` simplement crida la versió més "
"completa amb alguns arguments per defecte. El significat exacte d'aquests "
"valors queda fora de l'abast d'aquest tutorial; consulteu la pàgina sobre "
"la :ref:`classe Object <doc_object_class>` per obtenir més detalls sobre la "
"vinculació de mètodes i propietats."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1149
msgid ""
"The complete version is more involved. First, it creates ``String``'s and "
"``StringName``'s for the needed fields, by allocating memory and calling "
"their constructors. Then it creates a ``GDExtensionPropertyInfo`` struct and "
"sets all the fields with the arguments provided. Finally it returns this "
"created struct."
msgstr ""
"La versió completa és més elaborada. Primer crea ``String``\\ s i "
"``StringName``\\ s per als camps necessaris, assignant memòria i cridant els "
"seus constructors. Després crea un struct ``GDExtensionPropertyInfo`` i "
"estableix tots els camps amb els arguments proporcionats. Finalment retorna "
"l'struct creat."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1154
msgid ""
"The ``destruct_property()`` function is straightforward, it simply calls the "
"destructors for the created objects and frees their allocated memory."
msgstr ""
"La funció ``destruct_property()`` és directa: simplement crida els "
"destructors dels objectes creats i allibera la memòria assignada."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1157
msgid ""
"Let's go back again to the header ``api.h`` to create the functions that "
"will actually bind the methods:"
msgstr ""
"Tornem un altre cop a la capçalera ``api.h`` per crear les funcions que "
"vincularan realment els mètodes:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1177
msgid "Then switch back to the ``api.c`` file to implement these:"
msgstr "Després torneu al fitxer ``api.c`` per implementar-les:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1264
msgid ""
"Both functions are very similar. First, they create a ``StringName`` with "
"the method name. This is created in the stack since we don't need to keep it "
"after the function ends. Then they create local variables to hold the "
"``call_func`` and ``ptrcall_func``, pointing to the helper functions we "
"defined earlier."
msgstr ""
"Totes dues funcions són molt semblants. Primer creen un ``StringName`` amb "
"el nom del mètode. Es crea a la pila perquè no cal conservar-lo després que "
"acabi la funció. Després creen variables locals per contenir ``call_func`` i "
"``ptrcall_func``, que apunten a les funcions auxiliars que hem definit abans."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1269
msgid ""
"In the next step they diverge a bit. The first one creates a property for "
"the return value, which has an empty name since it's not needed. The other "
"creates an array of properties for the arguments, which in this case has a "
"single element. This one also has an array of metadata, which can be used if "
"there's something special about the argument (e.g. if an ``int`` value is 32 "
"bits long instead of the default of 64 bits)."
msgstr ""
"Al pas següent divergeixen una mica. La primera crea una propietat per al "
"valor de retorn, que té un nom buit perquè no cal. L'altra crea un array de "
"propietats per als arguments, que en aquest cas té un sol element. Aquesta "
"també té un array de metadades, que es pot usar si hi ha alguna cosa "
"especial sobre l'argument (per exemple, si un valor ``int`` té 32 bits en "
"comptes dels 64 bits per defecte)."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1276
msgid ""
"Afterwards, they create the ``GDExtensionClassMethodInfo`` with the required "
"fields for each case. Then they make a ``StringName`` for the class name, in "
"order to associate the method with the class. Next, they call the API "
"function to actually bind this method to the class. Finally, we destruct the "
"objects we created since they aren't needed anymore."
msgstr ""
"Després creen el ``GDExtensionClassMethodInfo`` amb els camps necessaris per "
"a cada cas. Tot seguit creen un ``StringName`` per al nom de la classe, per "
"associar el mètode amb la classe. A continuació criden la funció de l'API "
"per vincular realment aquest mètode a la classe. Finalment, destruïm els "
"objectes que hem creat, ja que ja no calen."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1283
msgid ""
"The bind helpers here use the call helpers we created earlier, so do note "
"that those call helpers only accept the Godot ``FLOAT`` type (which is "
"equivalent to ``double`` in C). If you intend to use this for other types, "
"you would need to check the type of the arguments and return type and select "
"an appropriate function callback. This is avoided here only to keep the "
"example from becoming even longer."
msgstr ""
"Els auxiliars de vinculació d'aquí usen els auxiliars de crida que hem creat "
"abans, així que tingueu en compte que aquests auxiliars de crida només "
"accepten el tipus ``FLOAT`` de Godot (que equival a ``double`` en C). Si "
"voleu usar això per a altres tipus, hauríeu de comprovar el tipus dels "
"arguments i el tipus de retorn i seleccionar un callback de funció apropiat. "
"Aquí s'evita només per impedir que l'exemple sigui encara més llarg."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1290
msgid ""
"Now that we have the means to bind methods, we can actually do so in our "
"custom class. Go to the ``gdexample.c`` file and fill up the "
"``gdexample_class_bind_methods()`` function:"
msgstr ""
"Ara que tenim els mitjans per vincular mètodes, ja podem fer-ho realment a "
"la nostra classe personalitzada. Aneu al fitxer ``gdexample.c`` i ompliu la "
"funció ``gdexample_class_bind_methods()``:"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1305
msgid ""
"Since this function is already being called by the initialization process, "
"we can stop here. This function is much more straightforward after we "
"created all the infrastructure to make this work. You can see that "
"implementing the binding functions inline here would take some space and "
"also be quite repetitive. This also makes it easier to add another method in "
"the future."
msgstr ""
"Com que aquesta funció ja la crida el procés d'inicialització, podem aturar-"
"nos aquí. Aquesta funció és molt més directa després d'haver creat tota la "
"infraestructura perquè això funcioni. Podeu veure que implementar aquí les "
"funcions de vinculació en línia ocuparia espai i també seria força "
"repetitiu. Això també facilita afegir un altre mètode en el futur."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1311
msgid ""
"If you compile the code and reopen the Godot project, nothing will be "
"different at first, since we only added two new methods. To ensure those are "
"registered properly, you can search for ``GDExample`` in the editor help and "
"verify they are present in the documentation page."
msgstr ""
"Si compileu el codi i torneu a obrir el projecte de Godot, al principi no hi "
"haurà res de diferent, ja que només hem afegit dos mètodes nous. Per "
"assegurar-vos que s'han registrat correctament, podeu cercar ``GDExample`` a "
"l'ajuda de l'editor i verificar que són presents a la pàgina de documentació."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1320
msgid "Custom properties"
msgstr "Propietats personalitzades"

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1322
msgid ""
"Since we now have the getter and setter for our properties already bound, we "
"can move forward to create actual properties that will be displayed in the "
"Godot editor inspector."
msgstr ""
"Com que ara ja tenim vinculats el getter i el setter de les nostres "
"propietats, podem avançar i crear propietats reals que es mostraran a "
"l'inspector de l'editor de Godot."

#: ../../docs/engine_details/engine_api/gdextension/gdextension_c_example.rst:1326
msgid ""
"Given our extensive setup in the previous section, there are only a few "
